{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_31", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'git diff --check; git status --short; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'", "aggregated_output": " M cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_alu.py\n# Shared combinational radix-4 divider\n\nImplemented the hypothesis locally in `rtl/alu.sv`. DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU\nshare one unsigned magnitude divider with sixteen generated stages.\nEach stage consumes the next dividend pair, computes three 35-bit\nunsigned trial subtractions in parallel, and selects the remainder\nwith exclusive digit predicates and a masked-OR mux. D, 2D, and 3D\nare formed once at 34 bits. Quotient digits directly fill the 32-bit\nquotient; the final stage supplies the remainder. Signed operations\nnormalize operands and restore the quotient/remainder signs. The\nexisting explicit zero-divisor and INT_MIN/-1 overrides are retained.\n\nThe divider declarations and network are excluded under\n`RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS`; every ALTOPS substitution remains byte-for-byte\nunchanged. Multiplication, other ALU operations, module interfaces,\ncombinational latency, pipeline registers, and stall logic are unchanged.\n\nExtended `test/test_alu.py` while retaining all existing checks. Added\n13,452 directed operand pairs and 20,480 deterministic random pairs;\neach pair checks all four real division operations against independent\nPython integer arithmetic. Directed coverage includes zero divisors,\nsigned overflow, all sign combinations, high-bit divisors, powers of\ntwo, radix-4 quotient digits, and values below/equal/above divisor\nmultiples. Paired DUT results also check the quotient/remainder identity,\nremainder bounds, and signed remainder sign when applicable. Corrected\nstale test documentation that described a removed iterative FSM.\n\nLocal validation:\n\n- `make lint TARGET=bench`: PASS, no warnings. The requested unordered\n  `verilator ... cores/bench/rtl/*.sv` glob fails on the existing\n  compilation-unit typedef ordering (`core.sv` precedes `core_pkg.sv`).\n  The repository's lint target puts `core_pkg.sv` first as required by\n  its existing source comments and all canonical build flows.\n- Full cocotb suite: PASS (five pytest runners, 80 cocotb tests, including\n  26 ALU and eleven pipeline tests). The two added tests execute 135,728\n  division/remainder result comparisons over 33,932 operand pairs.\n- `make cosim TARGET=bench NRET=1`: PASS for selftest with and without\n  random instruction/data stalls and stalled canonical CoreMark CRCs.\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench JOBS=8 bash formal/run_all.sh`:\n  PASS on the first attempt: 53 passed, zero failed. No fixes or retries.\n  Uses the auto-detected single\n  retirement channel wrapper/configuration and ALTOPS.\n- `make timing TARGET=bench`: placement 0 PASS, Fmax 5.395 MHz,\n  6,111 logic cells, 460 registers, 151 reported logic levels.\n  Worst reported setup arrival: 190.652 ns, 442 cells, through\n  forwarding, execute, the ALU, and the result register.\n- `make fpga TARGET=bench NRET=1`: PASS for all three placements.\n  Placement Fmax values: [5.395, 5.998, 5.998] MHz; median 5.998 MHz,\n  versus baseline [5.140, 5.442, 5.442] MHz and median 5.442 MHz.\n  Median Fmax improves 10.22%; logic cells fall from 12,312 to 6,111\n  (50.37% reduction); register count remains 460. Reported fitness\n  improves from 12.12 to 13.35 CoreMark iterations/second.\n  Canonical stalled CoreMark completed ten iterations in exactly\n  4,491,485 bracketed cycles, equal to baseline. All five expected CRCs\n  and the validation literal passed. A separate call to the canonical\n  `run_coremark_ipc` helper confirmed the same bracketed cycle count\n  and 2.2264351322558128e-6 iterations/cycle.\n\nNo arithmetic implementation deviations from the hypothesis. The\nprincipal concern remains routing and borrow/sign-path delay: the ALU\nstill dominates the worst path despite the measured median improvement.\nPlacement sensitivity is visible in the 5.395 versus 5.998 MHz results.\nFast formal proves ALTOPS routing/control, not the real\ndivider arithmetic; real arithmetic is exercised by the expanded\ncocotb tests and cosim. The slow periodic `make formal-deep` suite was\nnot run during this iteration.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
