 stage can break\\nstalled execution, while registering complete decisions at existing\\nboundaries can improve timing without changing CoreMark cycles.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Split the existing execute-output boundary into independently captured\\ninteger-result payload and the established instruction-ownership/control\\ntoken. Keep one shared full-width EX/MEM result register, but giv\n…[97498 of 100570 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:4fa5c4e5581060e6]…\nt (div_result)\n  );\n\n  // ── Branch resolve ────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  logic [7:0]  nibble_equal, nibble_less, less_terms;\n  logic        branch_equal, unsigned_less, signed_less;\n  logic        branch_cond;\n  logic        branch_taken;\n  logic [31:0] branch_target;\n  logic [31:0] jump_target;\n  /* verilator lint_off UNUSEDSIGNAL */\n  logic [31:0] jalr_sum;  // bit 0 deliberately dropped per RV JALR spec\n  /* verilator lint_on UNUSEDSIGNAL */\n\n  // All local comparisons read the same forwarded operands in parallel.\n  // Each less-than term requires equality only in the more significant\n  // nibbles; fixed reductions avoid a serial comparison-result cascade.\n  for (genvar nibble = 0; nibble < 8; nibble++) begin : g_branch_nibble\n    assign nibble_equal[nibble] = rs1[nibble*4 +: 4] == rs2[nibble*4 +: 4];\n    assign nibble_less[nibble] = rs1[nibble*4 +: 4] < rs2[nibble*4 +: 4];\n  end\n  assign less_terms[7] = nibble_less[7];\n  assign less_terms[6] = nibble_equal[7]   & nibble_less[6];\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
