{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_63", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'git diff --check; git status --short; cmp cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv formal/riscv-formal/cores/bench-wEUAdJRAT/ex_stage.sv; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'", "aggregated_output": " M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_ex_stage.py\n# Branch comparison before forwarding selection\n\nChanged only `rtl/ex_stage.sv` and `test/test_ex_stage.py`.\n\nEX compares every pairing of EX/MEM ALU data, MEM/WB unified write data,\nand the two saved ID/EX source values before selecting branch predicates.\nThe EX/MEM-with-EX/MEM and MEM/WB-with-MEM/WB pairings use equality=true\nand signed/unsigned less-than=false constants. The saved-value pairing\nstill compares two independent values. Comparisons use native `==`, `<`,\nand `$signed(...) < $signed(...)` expressions.\n\nThe registered forwarding masks select one bit from the candidate predicate\nmatrix. The six legal operations and two reserved encodings retain their\nexisting results. Raw forwarding, complete ALU selections, arithmetic\ncapture, RVFI operands, alignment traps, forwarding permissions, successor\nverification, registered recovery, predictor feedback and all pipeline\nregister/stall ownership remain unchanged. Retirement remains nret=1.\n\nExisting tests are retained. Added directed and deterministic random tests\nfor all nine forwarding pairings and all eight branch encodings, including\nequality, sign/carry boundaries, taken-only misalignment, held instructions,\npredictor feedback and pending recovery. Added a Yosys SAT proof of the\nactual branch-condition cone against the original mux-then-compare reference\nfor arbitrary candidate values and every legal one-hot mask pair. Its\ntemporary observation port exists only in a scratch copy under TMPDIR.\n\nNo architectural deviations remain in the final RTL. Equivalent grouped\noperation decoding and relation-selection alternatives were explored, then\ndiscarded because their timing also missed acceptance. The final RTL uses\nthe hypothesis's explicit six-operation predicate decode and one-bit masked\nselection. Its source is byte-identical to the copy that passed CPU formal.\n\nLocal validation of the final version:\n\n- Verilator lint: pass, no warnings.\n- Full cocotb suite: 9 pytest tests passed (136 cocot\n…[1154 of 4226 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:3082cc220a5d1f8a]…\n ID/EX saved rs2 data, traverses a native speculative comparator,\npredicate selection and alignment-adjusted forwarding permission, and ends\nat an ID/EX operand-selection register. Ordinary ALU paths are also close\nto the limit.\n\nFitness computed with the canonical stalled bracket is 192.6261053\niterations/second, below both the champion's 223.44 and the required\n233.71824. This hypothesis is functionally correct but fails the local\nperformance acceptance criterion. Comparator replication increases area\nand routing enough to outweigh removing the full-width forwarding muxes\nfrom the branch comparison path.\n\nExplored alternatives also missed acceptance: grouped operations with row\nselection measured 73.561 MHz median; selecting three relation bits before\noperation decode measured 78.212 MHz; compact two-bit operation decoding\nmeasured 82.437 MHz. The literal implementation is retained to leave the\nproposed hypothesis directly reviewable; none of these variants approached\nthe required approximately 98.019 MHz.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
