{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_62", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md; cat cores/bench/rtl/reg_file.sv; cat cores/bench/generated/gowin_p0/impl/gwsynthesis/core_bench_syn_rsc.xml'", "aggregated_output": "# Flop register file and operand boundary\n\nOnly `rtl/reg_file.sv` and `test/test_reg_file.py` are changed. The module\ninterface and all pipeline RTL remain intact, including the existing ID/EX\noperand capture, hold/flush behavior, forwarding, skid buffer, predictor,\nblocking arithmetic, memory handshake, and single-channel retirement.\n\nThe register file contains 31 generate-local 32-bit words. Each has its own\nposedge process, synchronous zero reset, and write enable comparing against\na constant five-bit local address. There is no dynamically indexed storage.\nBoth asynchronous read ports decode their addresses into masked word\ncontributions, with a constant-zero x0 leaf, then reduce 32 leaves through\nseparate arrays of 16, 8, 4, and 2 nodes and a scalar fifth level. Read\npriority remains x0, matching enabled live write, stored word; reset does\nnot gate the combinational bypass.\n\nThe final tree pairs leaves from the upper and lower address halves first:\nlevel 1 combines leaves n and n+16, then successive levels combine n and\nn+8, n+4, n+2, and finally the two remaining nodes. This reduces address\nbits 4 through 0 instead of pairing neighboring word numbers first. It is\nstill a complete balanced 32-leaf, five-level masked OR tree per port.\nThis grouping is the only implementation deviation from the initial\nadjacent-pair formulation; it improves placement timing without changing\nany logical result, priority, stage, or latency.\n\nAll five original register-file tests and assertions are preserved. Three\nadditional tests cover every pair of read addresses after filling every\nword, both simultaneous and independent bypasses, back-to-back overwrites,\ndisabled writes, x0,