{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_39", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/rtl/*.sv; git diff --check; git status --short; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'", "aggregated_output": "- V e r i l a t i o n   R e p o r t: Verilator 5.047 devel rev v5.046-331-g2cd9b8df6 (mod)\n- Verilator: Built from 0.703 MB sources in 14 modules, into 0.343 MB in 4 C++ files needing 0.000 MB\n- Verilator: Walltime 0.034 s (elab=0.004, cvt=0.020, bld=0.000); cpu 0.034 s on 1 threads; allocated 24.285 MB\n M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_ex_stage.py\n M cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\n# Parallel carry-consistency successor verification\n\nChanged only `rtl/ex_stage.sv`, `test/test_ex_stage.py`, and\n`test/test_pipeline.py` (plus this requested, gitignored note).\n\nEX now infers each incoming carry from A XOR B XOR the captured prediction,\ncomputes outgoing carries independently through bit 30, and checks adjacent\ncarry relations with an explicit balanced five-level OR reduction. The\nsequential check uses PC and 4; the PC-relative check uses PC and the decoded\nimmediate. Decoded `is_jalr` selects the forwarded-rs1 check, which requires\nP[0]=0 and independently checks C[1] against A[0] AND B[0]. There is no\ncarry-out check for bit 31.\n\nActual target adders, actual branch comparison/outcome, alignment traps,\nlink values, architectural RVFI successors, advancement gating, registered\nEX/MEM recovery ownership and one-shot feedback are unchanged. The 64-entry\nfull-tag BTB, direction counters, fetch/skid behavior, stage widths,\nforwarding, M arithmetic/ALTOPS, bus handshakes and NRET=1 IO are unchanged.\nNo evaluation files or formal assumptions were changed.\n\nAdded standalone combinational Yosys SAT miters that extract the exact RTL\nhelper and prove its equivalence to full 32-bit modular addition equality\nfor ordinary and bit-zero