er owns EX, but let older EX/MEM\n  and MEM/WB instructions drain. Insert invalid, side-effect-free EX/MEM\n  bubbles while waiting; do not repeatedly hold and reissue an older\n  memory operation. Existing dmem backpressure still holds a pending older\n  memory request, and has priority over advancing EX/MEM. Accept a divide\n  only from a valid legal instruction when EX can start it; retain a\n  completed r\n…[3353 of 6425 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:69c5cacb5f2c1a69]…\nic randomized signed\n      and unsigned quotient/remainder comparisons, all sign combinations,\n      divide-by-zero and overflow corners, bounded completion, back-to-back\n      requests, result backpressure and reset during an operation. Keep\n      multiplication and ordinary combinational ALU coverage intact.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Add real-arithmetic end-to-end cases for ALU/load-to-divide forwarding,\n      divide-result consumers, dependent branches, back-to-back divides,\n      an older store/load draining during division, coincident imem/dmem\n      stalls and reset while busy. Assert exact single retirement, contiguous\n      rvfi_order, correct captured source operands, no duplicated accepted\n      stores, correct results and bounded progress; preserve existing tests.\n3:The structural hypothesis replaces combinational division with a blocking iterative divider to shorten the 199.837 ns critical path. Expected fitness gain: **50%**, pending implementation and measurement.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
