e for each possible acceptance pair of the next near and far\n  producer. Each choice already resolves youngest-writer priority\n  and includes the saved write-first RF fallback. If the near\n  producer is accepted and matches a nonzero source it wins; otherwise\n  an accepted matchi\n…[5368 of 8440 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:c6a528a750068bdb]…\nold semantics.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Wire decode candidate identities/static intents and registered\n      EX/MEM/MEM-WB acceptance to the new forwarding partition.\n      Keep all top-level ports, nret=1 retirement, hazards, memory\n      protocol and predictor/recovery latency unchanged.\n  - file: test/test_ex_stage.py\n    description: |\n      Adapt input packing without dropping existing assertions.\n      Cover every registered acceptance combination, matching near\n      and far writers, canceled near jump/far load, raw versus ALU\n      overrides, x0, held WB payload and saved M completion operands.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Preserve existing tests and add meaningful end-to-end canceled\n      producer fallback cases with same-rd older writers, both-source\n      dependencies, load-use bubbles, prolonged dmem/M holds and\n      coincident recovery. Check exact RVFI source values/results,\n      contiguous order, no wrong-path/duplicate effects and progress.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
