{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_12", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('.tmp/agent-logs/impl.hyp-20260930-002-r13s1.log')\nfor line in p.read_text().splitlines():\n    try: row=json.loads(line)\n    except ValueError: continue\n    item=row.get('item',{})\n    if item.get('type') == 'agent_message':\n        print(item.get('text',''))\n    if item.get('type') == 'command_execution':\n        output=item.get('aggregated_output','')\n        if any(x in output for x in ['226.61','fmax_mhz','critical_path']):\n            print(output[:6000])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "I’ll inspect the pipeline and tests, implement the registered MEM recovery lane and M cancellation, then run lint, unit tests, formal, and cosimulation within the time budget.\n\nname: bench\ndescription: Frozen LLM-benchmark fixture core. Identical RTL to baseline at the bench-fixture-v1\n  freeze point. The benchmark matrix clones from the bench-fixture-v1 orphan branch\n  and operates only on this directory.\nisa: rv32im\nnret: 1\ntarget_fpga: tang-nano-20k\ntargets:\n  fmax_mhz: 135\n  lut4: 10000\n  coremark_iter_s: 300\n  coremark_per_mhz: 2.2\ncurrent:\n  fmax_mhz: 93.708\n  lut4: 3584\n  ff: 1188\n  coremark_iter_s: 2.0e-06\n  coremark_per_mhz: 0.0\n  source_id: hyp-20260930-001-r9s0\n  updated: '2026-09-30T04:55:12.808850Z'\n.PHONY: help lint test test-infra cosim formal fpga timing next loop report bench clean\n.DEFAULT_GOAL := help\n\n# Resolve OSS CAD Suite path so commands work even when the user hasn't\n# sourced .toolchain/oss-cad-suite/environment in this shell.\nTOOLCHAIN_DIR := $(CURDIR)/.toolchain\nOSS_BIN       := $(TOOLCHAIN_DIR)/oss-cad-suite/bin\nLOCAL_BIN     := $(TOOLCHAIN_DIR)/bin\nexport PATH := $(OSS_BIN):$(LOCAL_BIN):$(PATH)\n\n# Orchestrator knobs (pass-through to tools.orchestrator):\n#   N        — number of rounds for `make loop` (default 10).\n#   K        — tournament size, slots per round (default 1 = sequential).\n#   AGENT    — codex (default) or claude. Honors a pre-existing\n#              AGENT_PROVIDER env var if AGENT isn't set on the make\n#              command line.\n#   BASE     — when forking a new TARGET, copy from cores/<BASE>/.\n#              Default: baseline (orchestrator-side default).\n#   COREMARK — target CoreMark iterations/sec (e.g. '370').\n#   LUT      — target LUT count (e.g. '3000').\n#   WORKTREE — default ON. `make loop` first creates a dedicated git worktree\n#              at .worktrees/<TARGET>/ on branch core-<TARGET> and re-execs\n#              itself there. Lets two `make loop` invocations for different\n#              TARGETs run in parallel without git index/merge collisions.\n#      \n…[17836 of 20908 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:0739e32fca8b9faf]…\ns\": -5.728,\n    \"arrival_ns\": 16.022,\n    \"logic_cells\": 12,\n    \"modules\": [\n      \"clock_ibuf\",\n      \"cpu/u_if\",\n      \"cpu/u_hazard\",\n      \"cpu/u_id\",\n      \"cpu/u_if\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06,\n  \"fitness\": 226.61,\n  \"cycles\": 4254623,\n  \"iterations\": 10\n}\n\nCosimulation passes. The first timing run reports 93.214 MHz, below the estimated frequency needed for acceptance; the leading paths are now in fetch skid control and the ALU. I’m measuring median fitness and finishing the annul and cancellation tests. Formal has reported no failures so far, but the register check is still running.\n\nFormal passed all 53 checks. Median vendor Fmax is 96.414 MHz over 4,254,623 marker cycles, yielding 226.61 iterations/second. That misses the 233.71824 acceptance threshold. The recovery cases pass; I’m finishing the full unit suite and recording the result.\n\n[implementation_notes.md](/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_1-sol_xhigh-v2-rep1/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260930-002-r13s1/cores/bench/implementation_notes.md)\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
