ndidate\nand the corresponding quotient digit 1, 2, or 3; select T and digit 0\nwhen all three borrow. Use mutually exclusive digit predicates and a\nparallel masked-OR remainder mux rather than a cascaded priority data\nmux. For nonzero D, every selected remainder is less than D and fits\n32 bits. Concatenate the sixteen two-bit digits to obtain the quotient,\nand use the final remainder directly, avoiding q*D remainder recovery.\nRestore the quotient sign using the dividend/divisor sign XOR and the\nremainder sign using the dividend sign. Explicit final overrides retain\ndi\n…[5192 of 8264 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:07e26dcce7a06b02]…\nad-use hazards and divider ownership. Use unchanged formal/cosim and\ncanonical stalled CoreMark CRC checks, plus vendor timing, to evaluate\ncorrectness and the proposed path reduction.\n\n{'id': 'hyp-20260929-002-r2s1', 'category': 'structural', 'title': 'Register the fetch/decode boundary to break EX redirect feedback', 'fitness': 98.3, 'fmax_mhz': 47.003, 'cycles': 4781572, 'critical_path': {'from': 'cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s', 'to': 'dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -14.898, 'arrival_ns': 25.193, 'logic_cells': 15, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}}\n{'id': 'hyp-20260929-003-r2s2', 'category': 'predictor', 'title': 'PC-indexed next-PC prediction with a short recovery control path', 'fitness': 119.03, 'fmax_mhz': 49.962, 'cycles': 4197447, 'critical_path': {'from': 'cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0', 'to': 'dmem_2_dmem_2_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -15.386, 'arrival_ns': 25.681, 'logic_cells': 15, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
