n prefix represents each\nsigned 32-bit value exactly. MUL uses bits 31:0, independent of signedness;\nMULH, MULHU and MULHSU use bits 63:32 with their respective sign modes.\nShare the identical high-half output arm. Do not apply a post-product\nsign correction, absolute-value normalization, partial-product adder\nnetwork, new pipeline register or blocking multiply latency.\n\nPreserve all four RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS constants and arithmetic formulas;\ntheir multiplication substitutes must use the same dedicated forwarded\nregister operands as real multiplication. For every valid decoded multiply\nthese equal the old a/b values, so routing and retirement semantics remain\nidentical. Keep DIV/REM real and abstract implementations, their request\nand result handshakes, capture metadata and backpressure behavior intact.\nKeep nret=1, all decoder legality/trap checks, alignment behavior, bus\nhandshakes, predictor policy and channel-0 RVFI ordering unchanged.\n\nAn isolated implementation of precisely this proposal reached 54.842 MHz\nwith Gowin placement option 0, versus the reproduced 49.053 MHz champion:\n11.8 percent faster for that option. Worst arrival fell from 25.681 to\n23.529 ns, DSP resources fell from six to two, and LUTs changed from\n2,998 to 3,027 with FFs unchanged at 871. The existing real-arithmetic\nALU and 23-test pipeline cocotb suites passed, including 41,296 extra\nmultiply checks covering directed chunk/sign boundaries and 10,000\nrandom operand pairs across all four multiplication operations.\n\nThe fitness prediction is a 10 percent gain at unchanged instruction\nlatency and bracketed cycles. Median timing and canonical stalled CoreMark\nmust confirm this; one placement result alone is not acceptance evidence.\nAt unchanged cycles, median Fmax must exceed 52.260252 MHz to clear fitness\n124.50538, the champion's 4.6 percent margin. Remaining forwarding, branch\ntraining, DSP sign-input and result-select paths can limit the gain.\nUse the existing formal/cosim gates, exact CoreMark CRC/UART/marker checks\nand all three Gowin placement options without changing evaluation files.\n''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':10,'confidence':'medium'},\n'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/alu.sv','description':'''Add dedicated forwarded-register multiply inputs. Replace mul_ss,\nmul_uu and mul_su with one signed 33-bit-by-33-bit product and exact\nper-operation sign-extension controls. Select its low/high halves as\nrequired. Route ALTOPS multiply substitutes through the same operands,\nretaining their exact constants/formulas. Preserve every nonmultiply\noperation and the divider state machine/interface behavior.\n'''},\n {'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Connect the multiplier inputs directly to the existing post-forwarding\nrs1/rs2 values, avoiding alu_a/alu_b's AUIPC/immediate muxes for multiply.\nKeep ordinary ALU/divider operand muxes, forwarding priorities, stage\nregisters, branch resolution, divider capture and RVFI metadata intact.\n'''},\n {'file':'test/test_alu.py','description':'''Drive the dedicated multiplier inputs in existing multiply checks and\nretain every existing ALU/divider assertion. Add sign and chunk-boundary\nvectors plus deterministic random exact comparisons for all four MUL\noperations against independent Python full-precision arithmetic. Also\ncheck multiply uses these dedicated operands when normal a/b differ,\nand nonmultiply operations continue to use their established inputs.\n'''},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Retain all pipeline checks and add directed multiply operand-routing\ncases for EX/MEM and MEM/WB forwarding, load-to-multiply dependencies,\nboth sources targeting one writer, and younger/older matching writers.\nExercise multiply consumers as stores, addresses and branches around\nimem/dmem stalls. Check exact high/low results, RVFI source values,\ncontiguous retirement order and accepted memory side effects.\n'''}]\n}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h,sort_keys=False,default_flow_style=False,width=88))\nprint('Refined hypothesis written:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Refined hypothesis written: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260929-001-r3s0.yaml\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
