{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_2", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"git status --short; rg -n 'predictor|prediction|branch|return.address|BTB|RAS' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "2:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260929-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Shared radix-4 combinational divider with parallel trial subtraction\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The baseline has a 199.837 ns, 156-cell worst path through forwarding,\\nthe execute-stage ALU, and the result register, and reaches only 5.442 MHz.\\nThe ALU expresses signed and unsigned quotient and remainder with four\\nseparate / and % operators. Deep combinational division is the strongest\\ncandidate for this path. Reducing its serial logic depth should raise\\nCoreMark iterations/second without adding instruction cycles or changing\\nthe existing memory-stall behavior. No earlier micro_opt attempts or\\ndistilled lessons exist for this fixture beyond the baseline retest.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The baseline has a 199.837 ns, 156-cell worst path through forwarding,\\nthe execute-stage ALU, and the result register, and reaches only 5.442 MHz.\\nThe ALU expresses signed and unsigned quotient and remainder with four\\nseparate / and % operators. Deep combinational division is the strongest\\ncandidate for this path. Reducing its serial logic depth should raise\\nCoreMark iterations/second without adding instruction cycles or changing\\nthe existing memory-stall behavior. No earlier micro_opt attempts or\\ndistilled lessons exist for this fixture beyond the baseline retest.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace only the real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU arithmetic in alu.sv with one\\nshared, fully combinational unsigned radix-4 quotient/remainder network.\\nNormalize signed DIV/REM operands to 32-bit unsigned magnitudes; unsigned\\noperations use the original operands. Consume the dividend two bits at\\na time, most significant pair first, in sixteen un