fwd\",\n        \"cpu/u_ex\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"from\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.alu_a_sel_0_s0\",\n      \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result_19_s0\",\n      \"slack_ns\": -7.116,\n      \"arrival_ns\": 17.41,\n      \"logic_cells\": 29,\n      \"modules\": [\n        \"clock_ibuf\",\n        \"cpu/u_ex\",\n        \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\",\n        \"cpu/u_ex\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"agent_message","text":"The result-selection probe also regressed. I’m choosing an unmeasured hypothesis based on the reproduced timing path: duplicate the registered forwarding buses for branch and address consumers to reduce fanout and routing delay. It preserves instruction latency and stall behavior."}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_43", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-001-r13s0.yaml')\np.write_text('''id: hyp-20260930-001-r13s0\ntitle: \\\"Replicate registered bypass buses for local execute consumers\\\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 223.44 at 93.708 MHz over 4,193,876 bracketed\n  CoreMark cycles. A fresh unchanged placement-option-0 build reproduces\n  92.907 MHz and its 16.058 ns worst path from MEM/WB.write_value[14]\n  through raw rs1 forwarding, branch/trap qualification and next-instruction\n  forwarding selection. That launch bit has fanout 10; its first route\n  alone costs 1.855 ns, followed by another 1.599 ns route into comparison.\n  Another near-critical ordinary-result path has ALU B bit-zero fanout 98.\n  The same producer words serve both complete ALU-input muxes and the raw\n  operand networks used by branches, JALR, addresses and stores.\n\n  LESSONS.md and the micro_opt history show that moving branch comparison,\n  writer permission or prediction verification has repeatedly exposed\n  another critical path. Local probes in this proposal worktree also\n  rejected carry-select target addition, shift-control preselection,\n  reordered shifts, result-capture factoring and operation predecode in\n  placement option 0. None established a gain. Their changes are excluded\n  from this hypothesis. Preserve the successful arithmetic and decision\n  networks and reduce the physical load on their common launch buses.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add one physically distinct registered copy of each existing 32-bit\n  near and far bypass word, at the same EX/MEM and MEM/WB clock boundaries.\n  Partition consumers: retain the original producer buses for complete\n  alu_a_sel/alu_b_sel operand muxes and blocking arithmetic capture; use\n  the copies for the raw rs1/rs2 muxes feeding branch comparison, JALR,\n  effective addresses, stores and RVFI source values. Both source networks\n  keep the existing registered one-hot forwarding selections and newest\n  writer priority. There is no new bypass decision or pipeline stage.\n\n  The near copy captures exactly the same next result as EX/MEM.alu_result:\n  fast integer/link result, saved MUL completion, saved DIV completion or\n  zero bubble, under the existing reset, dmem hold, redirect, completion\n  and ex_wait priorities. The far copy captures exactly the same unified\n  value as MEM/WB.write_value, including the load/ALU selection, and must\n  retain its payload on hold_wb even when retirement valid is cleared.\n  Reset initializes both copies consistently with the original words.\n  Never obtain a copy by sampling the original Q on the next clock edge;\n  both flops must sample the same D on the original capture edge.\n\n  Declare each copy as a separate local register with Gowin-supported\n  syn_preserve/syn_keep attributes as appropriate. Confirm in the mapped\n  vendor netlist that both 32-bit copies survive register merging and\n  have separate consumer nets. A wire alias or a duplicate RTL assignment\n  optimized back into one flop is not this experiment. Replicate storage,\n  not the multiplier, divider, arithmetic operators or control logic.\n  Share each established next-result expression between the original and\n  its copy so replication adds register load without duplicating arithmetic.\n\n  Add internal execute/memory output ports and top-level wiring for the\n  replicated words. The core's external IO and nret=1 RVFI ports remain\n  exact. Arithmetic operands, forwarded source bits, alignment traps,\n  producer permissions, predictor contents/training, registered recovery,\n  load-use bubbles and all request/completion timing remain unchanged.\n  In particular, held consumers must see the retained far copy during\n  dmem stalls, and M completion must update the original and near copy\n  together before a dependent instruction advances. Preserve wrong-path\n  store/M squash, once-only memory effects and contiguous retirement.\n\n  This is a local fanout and routing micro-optimization, not a prediction\n  policy or pipeline topology change. It adds 64 payload flops while\n  retaining identical valid-cycle behavior and CoreMark cycles. Smaller\n  producer fanout should let Gowin place raw-operand launch flops closer\n  to branch/address logic and keep ALU launch flops nearer integer logic.\n  The benefit is a hypothesis, not a measured timing result. A predictor\n  path may take over, and added clock/D-input load may erase the gain.\n\n  Predict six percent fitness improvement with low confidence. Acceptance\n  requires actual fitness above 233.71824; at 4,193,876 cycles this means\n  median vendor Fmax above approximately 98.02 MHz. Check copy/original\n  equality over reset, valid tokens, bubbles, holds and M completions;\n  run unchanged formal/cosim and canonical stalled CoreMark CRC, UART,\n  bounds and marker checks. Measure all scored placement options and\n  reject replication that disappears in synthesis or fails to improve\n  the measured median. Do not weaken any existing correctness check.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Add a preserved 32-bit near-result replica sampling the same next\n      result and priorities as EX/MEM.alu_result. Expose it internally.\n      Feed raw rs1/rs2 selection from replica inputs while keeping complete\n      ALU operand muxes on original buses. Preserve every trap, arithmetic,\n      token transition, recovery and request/completion equation.\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Add a preserved 32-bit far-result replica sampling the same load/ALU\n      value as MEM/WB.write_value on the same edge. Reset consistently and\n      retain data on hold_wb independently of retirement valid. Expose the\n      registered copy for raw-operand forwarding without another mux stage.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Wire the new near/far copy outputs back to execute's raw-operand\n      inputs. Keep original EX/MEM and MEM/WB words on ALU forwarding.\n      Preserve all external ports, hazard/permission wiring and RVFI logic.\n  - file: test/test_ex_stage.py\n    description: |\n      Retain all existing assertions. Drive matching original/replica\n      source words for established tests and check near-copy equality\n      across fast/link instructions, reset, bubbles, redirects, long\n      dmem stalls and exact MUL/DIV completion acceptance.\n  - file: test/test_mem_stage.py\n    description: |\n      Retain existing memory/alignment checks. Verify far-copy equality\n      for ALU results and all load widths, then verify payload retention\n      while hold_wb clears valid over consecutive stalled cycles.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Preserve every existing check. Exercise same-rd newest-writer cases,\n      consumers using both bypass sources, load-to-branch/JALR/store,\n      M-result consumers and pending recovery with both bus stalls.\n      Check exact RVFI sources/results/order and once-only memory effects.\n''')\nimport json, yaml, jsonschema\nh=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\njsonschema.validate(h,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nassert h['id']=='hyp-20260930-001-r13s0'\nassert h['category']=='micro_opt'\nassert type(h['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct']) is int\nassert -50 <= h['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct'] <= 50\nprint('Final hypothesis schema valid:',p)\nprint('Expected fitness delta:',h['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct'],'percent; confidence:',h['expected_impact']['confidence'])\nPY\ngit status --short\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
