{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n x=json.loads(line)\n if x.get('id') in ['hyp-20260930-001-r7s0','hyp-20260930-002-r8s1','hyp-20260930-003-r13s2']:\n  h=x['hypothesis']; print(x['id']); print(h['hypothesis']); print('changes:',h['changes'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20260930-001-r7s0\nSpecialize the existing EX/MEM memory-address datapath. Add a dedicated\n32-bit effective_addr register field fed directly by the existing ALU\naddition lane, before generic operation/result selection. For valid\nLOAD/STORE instructions its operands are exactly the already forwarded\narchitectural rs1 and decoded immediate. Drive every MEM\naddress consumer from that field instead of the general alu_result:\nio_dmemAddr, byte-lane masks, load extraction position, memory-alignment\nchecks, and the aligned RVFI memory address. Keep alu_result as the normal\nALU/branch-link/M result for writeback and EX/MEM forwarding. Loads continue\nto select their extended memory data into MEM/WB.write_value, while stores\ncontinue to use the original separately forwarded rs2 value.\n\nExpose an internal add_result = a + b output from alu and use this same\nnamed sum in the ordinary ALU_ADD result arm. Both consumers must share\nthe existing adder, retaining the existing ALU operand selection. The\naddress capture bypasses binary ALU operation/result selection, jump-link\noverride, and blocking M-result selection; do not duplicate the adder or\nadd another forwarding mux. Use full 32-bit modular rs1 + imm arithmetic, including all upper\nbits and low alignment bits; do not truncate to the FPGA RAM address width,\npre-align requests, specialize to CoreMark addresses, or change the allowed\nmemory map. A valid legal LOAD/STORE has alu_src=1 and is_auipc=0, so this\nvalue is bit-identical to its existing ALU_ADD effective address.\n\nClock effective_addr at the same EX/MEM boundary with the existing dmem\nhold enable. Retain it while stall is asserted, so every pending LOAD/STORE\npresents stable address, data and masks until acceptance. Give this field\nits own next-state assignment after the normal EX/MEM bundle assignment:\non each nonreset, nonstalled edge capture alu_add_result, independently of\nex_wait, M ownership/completion, recovery, fast opcode or instruction\nvalidity. Reset may clear it. The field is meaningful only for a vali\n…[19678 of 22750 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:14235f0ebbc54f3f]…\nification and use it\\nfor sequential, PC-relative and bit-zero-cleared JALR mismatch\\nchecks. Preserve full target arithmetic, architectural successors,\\nalignment traps, actual outcomes, registered recovery and feedback,\\nM ownership, forwarding and all advancement/hold/squash priorities.\\n'}, {'file': 'test/test_ex_stage.py', 'description': 'Retain all existing assertions and add meaningful exact-successor\\nverification vectors: long carries, wraparound, negative immediates,\\nevery predicted bit error, odd/even JALR sums and bit-one carry from\\nbit zero. Compare recovery decisions/targets with full-width sums\\nunder advancement, bubble, dmem hold and M completion conditions.\\n'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Retain pipeline checks and exercise forwarded JALR operands, changing\\nindirect targets, taken/not-taken loops, stale ordinary/illegal/M\\npredictions, full-skid recovery and both bus stalls. Check exact RVFI\\nPCs/order/traps/link writes and no younger register/store/M effects.\\n'}]\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
