{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nids={'hyp-20260930-001-r10s0','hyp-20260930-001-r11s0','hyp-20260930-001-r12s0','hyp-20260930-001-r13s0','hyp-20260930-001-r7s0','hyp-20260930-002-r8s1'}\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n x=json.loads(line)\n if x.get('id') in ids:\n  print(x['id'], x['title'])\n  print(x.get('motivation',''))\n  h=x['hypothesis']; print(h['hypothesis'] if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20260930-001-r7s0 Split and predecode EX result steering for arithmetic and memory addresses\nThe champion's registered one-hot bypass choices raised median Gowin Fmax\nto 74.535 MHz at 4,130,235 bracketed CoreMark cycles, but the remaining\nworst path still starts at MEM/WB.write_value[17], crosses EX and the\ngeneral ALU, and ends at a data-memory BSRAM input: 19.124 ns and thirteen\ncells. The memory interface currently takes its effective address from\nthe shared EX/MEM.alu_result bus, so arbitrary shift, compare, multiply\ncompletion and ALU-result selection circuitry can constrain the physical\nRAM address path even though loads/stores only require rs1 + immediate.\nPrior register-file and complete bypass-mask improvements make that\nunnecessary coupling the most promising remaining local micro_opt.\n\nSpecialize the existing EX/MEM memory-address datapath. Add a dedicated\n32-bit effective_addr register field fed directly by the existing ALU\naddition lane, before generic operation/result selection. For valid\nLOAD/STORE instructions its operands are exactly the already forwarded\narchitectural rs1 and decoded immediate. Drive every MEM\naddress consumer from that field instead of the general alu_result:\nio_dmemAddr, byte-lane masks, load extraction position, memory-alignment\nchecks, and the aligned RVFI memory address. Keep alu_result as the normal\nALU/branch-link/M result for writeback and EX/MEM forwarding. Loads continue\nto select their extended memory data into MEM/WB.write_value, while stores\ncontinue to use the original separately forwarded rs2 value.\n\nExpose an internal add_result = a + b output from alu and use this same\nnamed sum in the ordinary ALU_ADD result arm. Both consumers must share\nthe existing adder, retaining the existing ALU operand selection. The\naddress capture bypasses binary ALU operation/result selection, jump-link\noverride, and blocking M-result selection; do not duplicate the adder or\nadd another forwarding mux. Use full 32-bit modular rs1 + imm arithmetic, including all upper\nbits and low \n…[24814 of 27886 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:e141333b743ae260]…\nnd routing micro-optimization, not a prediction\npolicy or pipeline topology change. It adds 64 payload flops while\nretaining identical valid-cycle behavior and CoreMark cycles. Smaller\nproducer fanout should let Gowin place raw-operand launch flops closer\nto branch/address logic and keep ALU launch flops nearer integer logic.\nThe benefit is a hypothesis, not a measured timing result. A predictor\npath may take over, and added clock/D-input load may erase the gain.\n\nPredict six percent fitness improvement with low confidence. Acceptance\nrequires actual fitness above 233.71824; at 4,193,876 cycles this means\nmedian vendor Fmax above approximately 98.02 MHz. Check copy/original\nequality over reset, valid tokens, bubbles, holds and M completions;\nrun unchanged formal/cosim and canonical stalled CoreMark CRC, UART,\nbounds and marker checks. Measure all scored placement options and\nreject replication that disappears in synthesis or fails to improve\nthe measured median. Do not weaken any existing correctness check.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
