{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_40", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-001-r15s0.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20260930-001-r15s0\ntitle: \"Bank predictor payload into sixteen-word distributed RAMs\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 223.44 iterations/second at 93.708 MHz over\n  4,193,876 bracketed CoreMark cycles. Complete operand preselection and\n  grouped shifts already improved the execute datapath. Recent branch\n  comparator, recovery-retiming and bypass-replication attempts regressed.\n  Fresh isolated four-bit and eight-bit carry-select execute additions\n  also regressed, so retain the native arithmetic.\n\n  The existing predictor uses asynchronous reads of sixty-four-word tag\n  and target arrays without distributed-RAM banking. The proven r5s0\n  register-file change gained 9.16 percent by using explicit sixteen-word\n  distributed-RAM banks with reset validity. Apply that physical storage\n  mapping to the unchanged predictor payload. Earlier predictor experiments\n  changed policy or used registers/associative lookup; this proposal retains\n  the existing direct indexing, full tags and exact prediction behavior.\nhypothesis: |\n  Reimplement only the physical storage of if_stage's existing 64-entry\n  tagged next-PC table as four directly indexed 16-word distributed-RAM\n  banks. This is a micro-optimization of memory inference and local routing,\n  with no predictor capacity, policy, pipeline stage or latency change.\n\n  Pack each entry into 57 bits: tag[23:0], target[29:0], unconditional\n  and the two-bit saturating counter. Declare four [0:15] payload arrays\n  with Gowin's syn_ramstyle=\"distributed_ram\" attribute. The lower four\n  index bits address each bank and the upper two select one bank through\n  an explicit flat four-way read selection. Provide both the fetch-index\n  read and training-index read. Let synthesis replicate storage needed\n  for coherent asynchronous read ports; never introduce a read register\n  or an extra feedback cycle. Only the selected bank writes on each\n  existing valid allocating training edge, with all packed fields\n  captured together. Do not reset payload RAM or imp\n…[3139 of 6211 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:9db09acb129e4d00]…\n    reset and skid/recovery behavior without another cycle or bypass.\n  - file: test/test_if_stage.py\n    description: |\n      Retain existing assertions and verify predictions against an\n      independent 64-entry reference table across every bank and row,\n      independent fetch/training indices, collisions, back-to-back writes,\n      counter boundaries, unconditional targets, invalidation and reset.\n      Exercise stalls, full-skid replacement and recovery while training;\n      check exact pre-edge prediction and token acceptance semantics.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Preserve all full-core checks and cover control sites in different\n      banks and colliding tags, with independent imem/dmem holds and\n      recovery during a full skid entry. Require exact architectural\n      successors, ordered retirement and once-only memory/M effects.\n      Existing arithmetic, legality and canonical CoreMark gates remain\n      mandatory; do not change the test harness or benchmark contract.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
