EX.rd for next-cycle EX/MEM forwarding, and current EX/MEM.rd for\n  next-cycle MEM/WB forwarding. Include producer rd != 0 in each\n  comparison. Register these four Boolean results alongside ID/EX\n  using precisely its existing !stall payload enable. Reset them to\n  zero. They \n…[6036 of 9108 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:577c36005358103f]…\n_wb/reset semantics; dmem still uses EX/MEM addresses.\n  - file: rtl/wb_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Drive w_data directly from the unified MEM/WB alu_result slot.\n      Keep existing valid/reg_write write-enable and destination logic.\n      Update documentation to reflect selection before the MEM/WB edge.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Retain every existing assertion. Add cases with two older writers\n      to the same rd, both source ports, immediate-bit false dependencies,\n      x0, trapped producers and load consumers, then combine them with\n      prolonged dmem holds, imem outages, load-use bubbles and blocking\n      M completion followed immediately by a dependent consumer. Cover\n      all signed/unsigned load widths and load/ALU writebacks back to back.\n      Verify\n      exact RVFI sources/results/PCs, contiguous order and once-only\n      memory effects. Run unchanged formal, zero-wait/stalled random\n      trace cosim, canonical CRC/marker checks and median Gowin timing.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
