{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_68", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-001-r7s0.yaml');d=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Split and predecode EX result steering for arithmetic and memory addresses'\nd['hypothesis']+='''\nComplete this single EX result-steering specialization by predecoding the\nordinary writeback result before ID/EX. Add a twelve-bit fast_sel field:\nbits 0..10 select ADD, SUB, AND, OR, XOR, SLT, SLTU, SLL, SRL, SRA, LUI;\nbit 11 selects the JAL/JALR PC+4 link. Generate an exclusive mask from\nvalidated decoder outputs in ID, capturing it under the existing \"'!stall\npayload enable. Illegal instructions and M operations select no fast lane.\nReset clears the mask; holds retain it. Flush kills existing validity and\nside-effect controls without putting recovery on these mask payload flops.\nNo architectural effect may depend on an invalid mask.\n\nIn alu, select ordinary result lanes with parallel masked OR using those\nregistered bits, replacing binary fast-operation result steering. Reuse\nadd_result for its ADD lane, with the same expressions and signedness for\nall other operations. In EX OR the bit-11-masked PC+4 link with this fast\nresult, avoiding a late is_jump result mux. Existing dedicated M completion\nports still supply exact MUL/DIV results to the original saved-instruction\ncompletion path; preserve every real and ALTOPS formula and handshake.\nRetain the existing operand forwarding and PC/immediate operand muxes.\nThe shared addition lane always feeds effective_addr regardless of the\nfast-result mask, including on M/bubble cycles where no memory request is\nvalid. This specializes the two consumers of the same EX result network:\nmemory uses the unselected shared sum, while ordinary writeback uses a\npredecoded selector. Do not add separate arithmetic units or pipeline stages.\n'\"'''\nd['changes'][0]['description']+='\\\\nAdd the documented twelve-bit fast_sel field to id_ex_t; keep all existing raw\\\\nsource, forwarding, control and retirement fields intact.'\nd['changes'].insert(1,{'file':'rtl/id_stage.sv','description':'''Capture exclusive validated fast-result/link masks before ID/EX using its\nexisting payload enable. Preserve masks on holds, clear them on reset and\nannul their architectural effects through existing validity/control kills\non recovery/bubbles. Keep recovery off the mask payload capture logic.'''} )\nfor c in d['changes']:\n if c['file']=='rtl/ex_stage.sv': c['description']+='\\\\nConsume fast_sel through the ALU and flatten the jump-link override into its\\\\nparallel result OR. Keep the original M completion path and operand muxes.'\n if c['file']=='rtl/alu.sv': c['description']+='\\\\nAccept registered fast-result enables through an internal port and use\\\\nparallel masked-OR fast selection. M arithmetic correctness remains checked\\\\nthrough the existing dedicated result handshakes and completion ports.'\n if c['file']=='test/test_alu.py': c['description']+='\\\\nAdapt explicit fast-result mask stimuli and verify every lane independently.\\\\nRetain every exact M arithmetic assertion on the completion result ports.'\nclass D(yaml.SafeDumper): pass\nD.add_representer(str,lambda du,s:du.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',s,style='|' if '\\\\n' in s else None))\np.write_text(yaml.dump(d,Dumper=D,sort_keys=False,width=90))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Final candidate is written and schema-valid.')\nPY\npython3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor\nfrom tools.eval.cosim import run_one,TRACE_STALL_MODES\nfrom tools.eval.fpga import run_coremark_ipc\nimport json\nwt='/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_1-sol_xhigh-v2-rep1';root=Path('/srv/hwebench/tmp/e2005e29/cd5ac3c3/r7s0_probe');sim=str(root/'obj_final/cosim_sim')\nelfs=[p for p in (Path(wt)/'bench/programs').glob('*.elf') if p.name\"'!='\"'coremark.elf']\nwith ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=8) as pool:\n results=[j.result() for j in [pool.submit(run_one,p,sim,wt,None,f) for p in elfs for f in TRACE_STALL_MODES]]\ncm=run_coremark_ipc(wt,sim)\n(root/'cosim_final_result.json').write_text(json.dumps({'trace':results,'coremark':cm},indent=2))\nprint(json.dumps({'trace_passed':all(r['passed'] for r in results),'coremark':cm}),flush=True)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
