{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_51", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-001-r8s0.yaml')\nh={\n'id':'hyp-20260930-001-r8s0',\n'title':'Capture complete ALU operand choices before ID/EX',\n'category':'micro_opt',\n'motivation':'''The champion reaches 192.51 iterations/second at 80.738 MHz median\nGowin Fmax and 4,193,876 bracketed CoreMark cycles. Its placement-0\ncritical path starts at saved ID/EX.rs1_val[11] and ends at\nEX/MEM.alu_result[29], with 19.233 ns arrival and fourteen cells.\nA fresh unchanged vendor build reproduces that report. It traverses\ntwo raw forwarding LUTs and then an AUIPC-versus-rs1 operand LUT before\nthe ALU. The second path starts at a forwarding selection, traverses\nthe analogous register-versus-immediate operand network, and reaches\nalu_result[0] at 19.210 ns. The accepted complete bypass masks removed\nwriter comparisons and priority from EX, but the later PC/immediate\nchoices remain serial with data forwarding. LESSONS.md and the\nmicro_opt history establish that register-file banking and complete\none-hot bypass selections are valuable, while match-only retiming and\nr7s0 result/address predecode did not improve the champion. Extend the\nsuccessful selection principle to these remaining operand muxes.\n''',\n'hypothesis':'''Apply one local micro-optimization: fuse forwarding and ALU operand-source\nselection into complete four-way one-hot choices captured at the\nexisting ID/EX boundary. EX then masks registered candidate data once\ninstead of selecting a forwarded register and subsequently selecting\nPC or immediate. Preserve the established five-stage pipeline, ordinary\ninstruction latency, load-use interlock, blocking M algorithms,\nregistered recovery, independent effective-address lane, predictor,\nfetch skid buffer, retirement boundary and nret=1 port contract.\n\nAdd two four-bit payload fields, alu_a_sel and alu_b_sel, to id_ex_t.\nBits 0, 1 and 2 select the next EX/MEM result, next MEM/WB unified value\nand saved write-first RF value respectively. Bit 3 selects the saved\ninstruction PC for operand A, and the decoded immediate for operand B.\nIn ID form alu_a_sel = dec_is_auipc ? 4'b1000 : {1'b0,fwd_rs1_sel}\nand alu_b_sel = dec_alu_src ? 4'b1000 : {1'b0,fwd_rs2_sel}. Capture both\nunder the existing \"'!stall payload enable, using the offered instruction'\"'s\nvalidated decoder outputs and the already complete forwarding priority.\nReset clears them with the existing bundle reset. Holds retain them.\nExisting flush/bubble validity and side-effect cancellation remains in\nforce; a killed token's unused selector payload may retain its value.\nA valid accepted token always carries exactly one selected source for\neach ALU operand.\n\nReplace the two late alu_a/alu_b conditional muxes in EX with parallel\nfour-term masked ORs of the selected registered data. For A the candidates\nare fwd_ex_mem, fwd_mem_wb, in.rs1_val and in.pc; for B they are\nfwd_ex_mem, fwd_mem_wb, in.rs2_val and in.imm. Do not feed these ALU\noperands through the old raw rs1/rs2 muxes first. Preserve the existing\nthree-bit raw forwarding masks and raw rs1/rs2 network for architectural\nRVFI source values, store data, branch conditions, JALR and the independent\nrs1 + immediate memory address. AUIPC must still report its architectural\nraw source fields independently of its PC arithmetic input, and immediate\ninstructions must retain the original raw rs2 metadata. Leave binary ALU\noperation/result selection and EX/MEM result/metadata priority unchanged.\n\nThe selector choices must follow the actual token across dmem holds,\nload-use bubbles, recovery and blocking M ownership. A load-use consumer\nrecomputes its choice when it finally captures; it never forwards a load\naddress as data. An M request captures the newly selected forwarded ALU\noperands once, and uses those captured operands throughout execution even\nas older forwarding producers drain. At completion the held ID/EX identity\nstill advertises the existing near producer for the next consumer.\nMEM/WB retains its unified data during stalls despite retirement-valid\nclearing. Preserve newest-writer priority, x0, write-first RF behavior,\nmisalignment write cancellation, exact real RV32M and ALTOPS results,\nfull-width modular arithmetic, recovery age and stable pending memory\nrequests. Invalid selectors cannot start M operations or create any write,\nmemory transaction, predictor update or retirement. All legality, memory,\nRVFI and fitness checks remain mandatory.\n\nA temporary prototype implements exactly these two new fields, their ID\ncapture and the two EX masked-OR operands; every other champion RTL module\nis unchanged. With the unchanged FPGA wrapper and timed stall generator,\nGowin placements 0/1/2 reach 87.658/87.839/87.839 MHz, giving 87.839 MHz\nmedian, 8.795 percent above the champion. Placement 0 reports 3,660 LUT4,\n1,188 FF, 32 RAM16, 7 BSRAM and 2 DSP resources; its worst path is\n16.702 ns and twelve cells from EX/MEM.alu_result[27] to\nEX/MEM.alu_result[7]. Verilator lint passes in both real and ALTOPS modes.\nThese are prototype results, not an accepted tournament evaluation.\n\nPredict nine percent higher fitness with medium confidence, through\nhigher Fmax at unchanged work per cycle. At 4,193,876 canonical marker\ncycles the measured prototype timing would imply 209.45 iterations/second.\nAcceptance requires the measured (new_Fmax / 80.738) /\n(new_cycles / 4193876) to exceed 1.046; unchanged cycles require more than\n84.451948 MHz and fitness above 201.36546. The additional mask fanout and\ndecoder-to-ID capture path, and remaining branch/result paths, are the\nmain risks. Complete the unchanged unit/formal/cosim and canonical stalled\nCoreMark CRC/marker gates and median vendor evaluation on the final RTL.\n''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':9,'confidence':'medium'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/core_pkg.sv','description':'''Add documented four-bit alu_a_sel and alu_b_sel fields to id_ex_t,\nwith near/far/saved/PC-or-immediate bit positions. Retain every existing\nraw source, forwarding, control, result and retirement field.'''},\n{'file':'rtl/id_stage.sv','description':'''Generate the complete ALU operand masks from the validated offered\ninstruction's is_auipc/alu_src decode and existing prioritized bypass\nchoices. Capture them under the current \"'!stall payload enable; preserve\nthem on holds and clear them on reset. Keep all original token-validity,\nflush, control-kill, load-use and forwarding-selection rules.'\"'''},\n{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Use the captured four-way masks to select ALU A and B directly from\nregistered near/far/saved/PC-or-immediate candidates with parallel\nmasked ORs. Preserve raw forwarded rs1/rs2 and every branch, JALR,\naddress, store and RVFI consumer. Keep existing ALU interfaces/arithmetic,\nM ownership, source capture, result selection, EX/MEM priority and\nregistered recovery exactly intact.'''},\n{'file':'test/test_ex_stage.py','description':'''Adapt packed ID/EX layout builders for the new masks and preserve all\nexisting valid-result and trap assertions. Exercise near/far/saved\nsources, PC and immediate overrides, negative offsets, wraparound,\nAUIPC, shifts and exact M request operand capture. Check raw source\nmetadata separately from ALU inputs and stable selectors through holds.'''},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Retain all monitors and adapt ID/EX layout references. Cover register\nand immediate consumers of both forwarding sources, newest-writer\npriority, x0/write-first reads, load-use release, AUIPC, and M results\nfeeding arithmetic and addresses. Combine imem/dmem stalls, recovery\nand M completion; require exact RVFI operands/results, contiguous order,\nstable requests and once-only effects. Run unchanged formal/cosim,\ncanonical CoreMark CRC/marker validation and median vendor timing.'''}]\n}\njsonschema.validate(h,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h,sort_keys=False,width=78,default_flow_style=False))\nprint('Rewritten and schema-valid:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
