_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':9,'confidence':'medium'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/core_pkg.sv','description':'''Add documented four-bit alu_a_sel and alu_b_sel fields to id_ex_t,\nwith near/far/saved/PC-or-immediate bit positions. Retain every existing\nraw source, forwarding, control, result and retirement field.'''},\n{'file':'rtl/id_stage.sv','description':'''Generate the complete ALU operand masks from the validated offered\ninstruction's is_auipc/alu_src decode and existing prioritized bypass\nchoices. Capture them under the current \"'!stall payload enable; preserve\nthem on holds and clear them on reset. Keep all original token-validity,\nflush, control-kill, load-use and forwarding-selection rules.'\"'''},\n{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Use the captured four-way masks to select ALU A and B directly from\nregistered near/far/saved/PC-or-immediate candidates with parallel\nmasked ORs. Preserve raw forwarded rs1/rs2 and every branch, JALR,\naddress, store and RVFI consumer. Keep existing ALU interfaces/arithmetic,\nM ownership, source capture, result selection, EX/MEM priority and\nregistered recovery exactly intact.'''},\n{'file':'test/test_ex_stage.py','description':'''Adapt packed ID/EX layout builders for the new masks and preserve all\nexisting valid-result and trap assertions. Exercise near/far/saved\nsources, PC and immediate overrides, negative offsets, wraparound,\nAUIPC, shifts and exact M request operand capture. Check raw source\nmetadata separately from ALU inputs and stable selectors through holds.'''},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Retain all monitors and adapt ID/EX layout references. Cover register\nand immediate consumers of both forwarding sources, newest-writer\npriority, x0/write-first reads, load-use release, AUIPC, and M results\nfeeding arithmetic and addresses. Combine imem/dmem stalls, recovery\nand M completion; require exact RVFI operands/results, contiguous order,\nstable requests and once-only effe