{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_64", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-001-r9s0.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20260930-001-r9s0\ntitle: \"Predecode integer ALU lanes and fuse bidirectional shift selection\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 209.45 at 87.839 MHz and 4,193,876 bracketed\n  CoreMark cycles. Its worst Gowin path goes from EX/MEM.alu_result[27]\n  to EX/MEM.alu_result[7] through the ALU in 16.702 ns. This descending\n  bit dependency suggests the forwarded right-shift/result-selection\n  path, although the detailed mapped report must confirm the operation.\n  Earlier micro_opt gains came from registering complete operand choices;\n  the sibling result-ownership repartition reached only 87.114 MHz.\n  Integer operation decoding and three separate shift expressions remain\n  local opportunities after the accepted operand preselection.\nhypothesis: |\n  Apply one cycle-neutral ALU micro-optimization: capture complete integer\n  execution-lane controls at ID/EX and use them to fuse bidirectional\n  shifting with parallel result selection. Retain binary alu_op for the\n  existing M-extension ownership and ALTOPS machinery. From the validated\n  decoder's alu_op, generate a mutually exclusive result mask for ADD,\n  SUB, AND, OR, XOR, SLT, SLTU, SHIFT and LUI, plus registered shift-left\n  and arithmetic-right controls. Capture these fields under the existing\n  ID/EX payload enable and hold them with the actual instruction. Illegal\n  and M operations select no integer lane. No new pipeline stage, RAW\n  stall, instruction latency or memory-handshake change is introduced.\n\n  Implement SLL/SRL/SRA with one explicit five-step right barrel shifter.\n  SLL reverses A's bits before the network and reverses the final result;\n  SRL uses A unchanged with zero fill; SRA uses A unchanged with fill\n  equal to A[31]. Each step shifts by its fixed 1/2/4/8/16 amount when\n  the corresponding B[4:0] bit is set. Fuse output reversal and SHIFT\n  lane qualification into the final masked-OR result assembly rather\n  than selecting a shift result and then entering a binary ALU case mux.\n  Keep full-width ADD/SUB and signed/unsig\n…[2774 of 5846 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:e496d3874c752136]…\nt_alu.py\n    description: |\n      Keep all assertions and supply the new control inputs. Verify every\n      shift amount for SLL/SRL/SRA on signed boundaries, walking bits and\n      deterministic random operands; check all ordinary lane results and\n      retain the exact real RV32M and stable-result handshake checks.\n  - file: test/test_ex_stage.py\n    description: |\n      Adapt packed payload builders while retaining every existing check.\n      Cover shift and integer lanes with near/far/saved operands, immediate\n      shifts, holds, flushes, x0, alignment traps and once-only M completion.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Adapt ID/EX layout references and retain all architectural assertions.\n      Exercise dependent left/logical-right/arithmetic-right shift chains,\n      all shift amounts, load/M-to-shift forwarding and combined bus stalls\n      and recovery. Require exact RVFI values/order and once-only effects;\n      run all unchanged correctness and canonical vendor fitness gates.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
