{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_11", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n r=json.loads(line)\n if r['id'] in ['hyp-20260929-002-r4s1','hyp-20260930-001-r10s0']:\n  print(json.dumps(r,indent=2))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20260929-002-r4s1\",\n  \"title\": \"Split operand forwarding from execution with a registered operand stage\",\n  \"category\": \"structural\",\n  \"motivation\": \"The champion scores 129.51 iterations/second at median Gowin Fmax\\n56.790 MHz over 4,384,920 bracketed CoreMark cycles. Registered blocking\\nmultiply and divide removed the earlier arithmetic limits. A fresh\\nmake timing TARGET=bench on the unchanged champion reproduces placement\\noption 0 at 56.745 MHz and exposes two nearly tied bottlenecks: the\\n22.917 ns register-file-to-predictor path and a 22.906 ns WB destination\\ncomparison/forwarding-to-ALU-to-dmem path. Other register-file-to-dmem\\npaths are 22.892 ns. Optimizing just predictor feedback would leave\\nthe memory-side paths limiting the clock.\\n\\nThe detailed report shows BRAM register-file clock-to-output followed\\nby ID bypass, EX forwarding/operand muxes and execution, all in one\\nclock interval. The worst WB path carries a forwarding-select change\\nthrough operand selection, the ALU and its result mux into dmem.\\nThe earlier structural IF/ID-register attempt lost 10.64 percent\\nbecause it added fetch latency while the execution path remained\\ncritical. The successful registered-multiplier lesson is to put the\\nboundary inside the actual arithmetic/operand path. This proposal\\napplies that separation to ordinary execution and branch resolution.\\n\",\n  \"hypothesis\": {\n    \"motivation\": \"The champion scores 129.51 iterations/second at median Gowin Fmax\\n56.790 MHz over 4,384,920 bracketed CoreMark cycles. Registered blocking\\nmultiply and divide removed the earlier arithmetic limits. A fresh\\nmake timing TARGET=bench on the unchanged champion reproduces placement\\noption 0 at 56.745 MHz and exposes two nearly tied bottlenecks: the\\n22.917 ns register-file-to-predictor path and a 22.906 ns WB destination\\ncomparison/forwarding-to-ALU-to-dmem path. Other register-file-to-dmem\\npaths are 22.892 ns. Optimizing just predictor feedback would leave\\nthe memory-side paths limiting the clock.\\n\\nThe de\n…[22480 of 25552 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:1d22aed3eb6999f9]…\nd once-only memory effects. Retain\\nevery formal, cosim and canonical CoreMark validation gate.\\n\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"outcome\": \"regression\",\n  \"fitness\": 201.6,\n  \"delta_pct\": -9.77,\n  \"vs_baseline\": 1563.37,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 84.549,\n  \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06,\n  \"cycles\": 4193876,\n  \"iterations\": 10,\n  \"lut4\": 3661,\n  \"ff\": 1188,\n  \"seeds\": [\n    82.221,\n    84.549,\n    84.549\n  ],\n  \"perturbations\": [\n    [\n      0,\n      82.221,\n      15\n    ],\n    [\n      1,\n      84.549,\n      15\n    ],\n    [\n      2,\n      84.549,\n      15\n    ]\n  ],\n  \"lutram\": 32,\n  \"bsram\": 7,\n  \"dsp\": 2,\n  \"critical_path\": {\n    \"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.write_value_1_s0\",\n    \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/redirect_target_5_s0\",\n    \"slack_ns\": -7.162,\n    \"arrival_ns\": 17.457,\n    \"logic_cells\": 41,\n    \"modules\": [\n      \"clock_ibuf\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"logic_levels\": 15,\n  \"formal_passed\": true,\n  \"cosim_passed\": true,\n  \"error\": null,\n  \"implementation_notes\": \"\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-30T05:42:15.859743Z\",\n  \"slot\": 0,\n  \"round_id\": 10\n}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
