ion with a\\nNOP before decoding, register-file address selection and load-use\\ncomparison. Redirect also clears the comp\n6:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260929-002-r2s1\", \"title\": \"Register the fetch/decode boundary to break EX redirect feedback\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The champion's blocking iterative divider removed the dominant arithmetic\\nchain and raised m\n…[18564 of 21636 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:de639a840bf57f4f]…\nchieves 223.44 iterations/second at 93.708 MHz over\\n4,193,876 bracketed CoreMark cycles. Its reported worst path runs from\\nMEM/WB.write_value through execute to ID/EX forwarding selection.\\nSeparating writer permission alone in r10s0 exposed forwarded operands\\nthrough control-target generation to redirect_target as the next limit.\\nr11s1 moved prediction validation after EX/MEM but left its result\\ncombinational thr\n40:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260930-003-r13s2\", \"title\": \"Validate predicted successors with parallel carry consistency\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The champion scores 223.44 at 93.708 MHz over 4,193,876 marker-bracketed\\nCoreMark cycles. Prior predictor experiments expose forwarded operands\\nthrough target addition and successor equality into registered recovery.\\nMoving equality into decode or after EX/MEM reduced Fmax; cached operand\\ncertificates twice exceeded the formal timeout. Preserve the current\\nprediction table, metadata and recovery boundaries and replace the\\narithmetic-depende\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
