{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"agent_message","text":"The complete prototype reaches 71.792 MHz median across Gowin’s three placement options, with unchanged CoreMark cycles and valid CRCs and markers. That implies about 173.83 iterations/sec, a 15.6% gain over the champion. I’m recording this result in the hypothesis, along with the stall and trap rules needed to reproduce it."}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_35", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-002-r6s1.yaml')\nnew='''id: hyp-20260930-002-r6s1\ntitle: \\\"Register complete bypass selections and unified writeback data\\\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 150.32 iterations/second at 62.085 MHz with\n  4,130,235 bracketed CoreMark cycles. Its worst Gowin path starts at a\n  MEM/WB destination-register bit, crosses forwarding and execute, and\n  ends in the fetch predictor. The prior structural flop-register-file\n  attempt exposed the same forwarding-to-ALU-to-dmem limit and reached\n  only 61.852 MHz. A complete operand stage previously failed stalled\n  random cosim, and registering IF/ID increased cycles without improving\n  timing. Retiming the bypass network at existing stage boundaries can\n  shorten both execution paths without adding any instruction latency.\n  A scratch prototype registering only potential dependency matches\n  passed eight trace-cosim runs and canonical CoreMark at unchanged cycles,\n  but measured only 61.981 MHz median. Its worst paths instead started at\n  producer write permission and the WB ALU/load-select bit. The proposed\n  structural change registers the complete bypass choice and its WB data\n  source, addressing those remaining serial decisions together.\nhypothesis: |\n  Retime the forwarding network at the existing ID/EX and MEM/WB\n  boundaries. Generate the complete forwarding decision in decode for\n  the instruction about to enter ID/EX. Register a three-bit one-hot\n  near/far/saved selection for each source alongside its saved RF value.\n  In execute, select each operand with a parallel masked OR of the\n  EX/MEM result, the registered unified MEM/WB result and the saved RF\n  value. Execute must have no live destination comparison, write-enable\n  qualification or priority encoding before its operand muxes. This is\n  one restructuring of the bypass control and data pipeline; keep the\n  banked distributed-RAM RF, pipeline depth, fetch skid buffer, predictor\n  policy, blocking M units and nret=1 interface.\n\n  On a consumer capture edge, the near producer is the instruction\n  actually entering EX/MEM, normally the current ID/EX instruction. The\n  far producer is the instruction actually entering MEM/WB, normally the\n  current EX/MEM instruction. Match the offered instruction's raw rs1/rs2\n  fields against those destination numbers, excluding x0, and combine\n  each match with the producer's actual next-state write permission before\n  registering the choice. Derive near permission from execute's\n  trap-adjusted control and validity, and far permission from memory's\n  trap-adjusted control and validity. A misaligned JAL/JALR or memory\n  access must not claim a forwarding slot. Resolve newest-writer priority\n  before capture; when the near writer is canceled, choose a matching\n  permitted far writer or the saved RF value. Retain the existing load-use\n  interlock so an unready load address can never become operand data.\n  A current WB producer is already covered by write-first RF reads during\n  consumer capture; it is not one of these next-cycle forwarding sources.\n\n  Move WB's load-versus-ALU data selection to the input of MEM/WB. Capture\n  one unified write_value = mem_to_reg ? extended_load : alu_result\n  alongside the destination and write permission. Both WB-to-RF and\n  WB-to-EX then use this registered value directly. Preserve any existing\n  payload fields needed by RVFI or direct tests; synthesis may prune\n  redundant fields. The timed WB-to-EX path must not contain the old\n  mem_to_reg selection mux. During dmem holds retain the unified result,\n  destination and producer metadata while clearing only retirement\n  validity, as the existing MEM/WB forwarding contract requires. Avoid\n  qualifying retained forwarding data with WB.valid.\n\n  Keep forwarding selections aligned with the actual consumer token.\n  Hold them and its RF values on dmem or blocking-EX backpressure; kill\n  validity and side effects on load-use bubbles and recovery. ID/EX,\n  EX/MEM and the retained MEM/WB payload remain stable during dmem holds,\n  so a previously selected source stays usable despite WB.valid clearing.\n  When a load-use bubble clears, recompute the retained frontend consumer's\n  selection against the load now entering WB. When an M result completes,\n  use the saved blocking instruction's identity and write permission as\n  the near producer for the simultaneously captured consumer. Existing M\n  ownership must still capture fully forwarded sources once at request\n  acceptance and use that capture while older producers drain; live\n  selections during the owned wait must not recapture data. Derive matches\n  from actual next producers for exceptional transitions; do not assume\n  every stage advances together. Reset clears token validity and selection\n  state, and invalid tokens cannot advertise a producer or start effects.\n\n  A concrete implementation uses decode-side forward_unit inputs\n  id_rs1/id_rs2, near_rd = id_ex.rd, far_rd = ex_mem.rd,\n  near_write = id_ex.valid && ex.ctrl_with_trap.reg_write and\n  far_write = ex_mem.valid && mem.ctrl_with_trap.reg_write. For each\n  source choose 3'b001 on a permitted nonzero near match, otherwise\n  3'b010 on a permitted nonzero far match, otherwise 3'b100. Capture\n  these six bits inside id_stage's existing \"'!stall payload update;\n  a flush/bubble can set them to the saved-value selection. The M owner\n  preserves its identity in ID/EX through completion, so these destination\n  inputs remain aligned in that implementation. Execute reads the captured\n  masks directly. Add write_value to mem_wb_t, assign it on ordinary MEM\n  advancement and leave it untouched by hold_wb. WB'\"'s w_data becomes a\n  direct read of write_value. Keep the rest of the proven pipeline intact.\n\n  There is no added pipeline stage, fast RAW bubble, live ALU-data bypass\n  into decode or extra arithmetic latency. Preserve decoder default-illegal\n  discipline, alignment traps, all RV32M and ALTOPS results, exact RVFI\n  source operands, channel-0 retirement order, memory-handshake stability\n  and once-only memory effects. All verification and fitness contracts\n  remain unchanged. Check in Gowin that the selection bits and unified\n  WB value are actual register boundaries and that EX paths start at\n  registered data or selections rather than unregistered tag comparison,\n  producer permission or WB result selection.\n\n  A temporary prototype of this complete topology was built in scratch\n  storage using the unchanged FPGA wrapper, stall generator and Gowin\n  evaluator. Placement options 0/1/2 reached 68.014/71.792/71.792 MHz,\n  giving 71.792 MHz median, 15.63 percent above the champion. Option 0\n  reports 3,518 logic cells, 1,015 registers, 32 RAM16s, 7 BSRAMs and\n  2 DSPs. Its worst path starts at the unified WB data register and\n  reaches dmem through operand selection and ALU, at 19.997 ns and\n  14 cells; the old destination-tag-to-forwarding path is removed.\n  All eight selftest/random1/random2/random3 trace-cosim cases passed,\n  including combined imem/dmem stalls. The unchanged run_coremark_ipc\n  evaluator validates canonical CRCs, UART, memory bounds and markers,\n  completing 10 iterations in exactly 4,130,235 bracketed cycles. Thus\n  prototype timing times IPC implies 173.83 iterations/second, about\n  15.6 percent above the 150.32 champion. These are prototype measurements,\n  not an accepted tournament result; full unit and formal gates remain\n  required during implementation. Predict 16 percent with medium\n  confidence. Preserve this topology rather than registering matches\n  alone, which did not improve fitness. Decode permission fanout, MEM\n  load extraction plus result selection, and remaining ALU/branch paths\n  are the main risks. Acceptance requires (new_Fmax / 62.085) divided\n  by (new_cycles / 4130235) to exceed 1.046; with unchanged cycles the\n  required median is 64.94 MHz.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 16\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: |\n      Add registered three-bit one-hot near/far/saved operand selections\n      to ID/EX and a unified registered write_value field to MEM/WB.\n      Keep architectural, control and RVFI payload fields correct.\n  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n    description: |\n      Move dependency matching and newest-writer priority to decode.\n      Compare offered raw source fields with next EX/MEM and MEM/WB\n      destinations, using actual trap-adjusted next-state permissions.\n      Exclude x0 and emit one-hot selections for ID/EX capture.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Capture complete forwarding choices with the corresponding token\n      and RF operands. Preserve them across stage holds; annul invalid\n      tokens on reset/flush/bubbles. Maintain write-first reads and\n      simultaneous completion-cycle consumer capture.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Consume registered selections with parallel masked operand muxes,\n      removing execute-side tag comparison and permission qualification.\n      Expose the next EX/MEM producer's actual write permission after\n      alignment-trap adjustment, including blocking completions. Preserve\n      ALU, branch, M ownership and captured RVFI semantics.\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Register the selected extended-load-or-ALU writeback value before\n      WB, and expose the next MEM/WB producer's actual trap-adjusted write\n      permission for decode. Retain unified data and forwarding metadata\n      on dmem holds while clearing retirement validity. Preserve memory\n      masks, alignment handling, stable payload and RVFI captures.\n  - file: rtl/wb_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Drive w_data directly from the unified MEM/WB write_value register,\n      removing combinational ALU/load selection from both WB bypass paths.\n      Preserve valid-qualified RF writes, destination and x0 rules.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Wire decode-side producer identities/permissions and captured\n      selections, and connect the unified WB source. Preserve load-use,\n      dmem/M hold and recovery priorities, all top-level ports, nret=1\n      and the existing single retirement boundary.\n  - file: test/test_ex_stage.py\n    description: |\n      Adapt packed layouts and source selection stimuli to three-bit\n      one-hot inputs while preserving all existing arithmetic, branch,\n      ownership, backpressure and RVFI assertions. Verify actual write\n      permissions, trap cancellation and once-only M operand capture.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Cover adjacent ALU chains, equal-rd writers, trap-canceled writers\n      with older fallback, load-to-ALU/branch/store dependencies,\n      M-completion consumers, both-source forwarding and x0. Combine\n      long imem/dmem/M holds with retained WB data. Check exact sources,\n      results, contiguous order, no duplicate memory effects and progress.\n      Preserve all existing tests and run unchanged formal, stalled random\n      cosim, canonical CoreMark and median Gowin timing.\n'''\nprint('*** Begin Patch')\nprint('*** Update File: '+str(p.resolve()))\nprint('@@')\nfor line in p.read_text().splitlines():print('-'+line)\nfor line in new.splitlines():print('+'+line)\nprint('*** End Patch')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
