eep the rest of the proven pipeline intact.\n\n  There is no added pipeline stage, fast RAW bubble, live ALU-data bypass\n  into decode or extra arithmetic latency. Preserve decoder default-illegal\n  discipline, alignment traps, all RV32M and ALTOPS results, exact RVFI\n  source operands, channel-0 retirement order, memory-handshake stability\n  and once-only memory effects. All verification and fitness contracts\n  remain unchanged. Check in Gowin that the selection bits and unified\n  WB value are actual register boundaries and that EX paths start at\n  registered data or selections rather than unregistered tag comparison,\n  producer permission or WB result selection.\n\n  A temporary prototype of this complete topology was built in scratch\n  storage using the unchanged FPGA wrapper, stall generator and Gowin\n  evaluator. Placement options 0/1/2 reached 68.014/71.792/71.792 MHz,\n  giving 71.792 MHz median, 15.63 percent above the champion. Option 0\n  reports 3,518 logic cells, 1,015 registers, 32 RAM16s, 7 BSRAMs and\n  2 DSPs. Its worst path starts at the unified WB data register and\n  reaches dmem through operand selection and ALU, at 19.997 ns and\n  14 cells; the old destination-tag-to-forwarding path is removed.\n  All eight selftest/random1/random2/random3 trace-cosim cases passed,\n  including combined imem/dmem stalls. The unchanged run_coremark_ipc\n  evaluator validates canonical CRCs, UART, memory bounds and markers,\n  completing 10 iterations in exactly 4,130,235 bracketed cycles. Thus\n  prototype timing times IPC implies 173.83 iterations/second, about\n  15.6 percent above the 150.32 champion. These are prototype measurements,\n  not an accepted tournament result; full unit and formal gates remain\n  required during implementation. Predict 16 percent with medium\n  confidence. Preserve this topology rather than registering matches\n  alone, which did not improve fitness. Decode permission fanout, MEM\n  load extraction plus result selection, and remaining ALU/branch paths\n  are the main risks. Acceptance requires (new_Fmax / 62.085) divided\n  by (new_cycles / 4130235) to exceed 1.046; with unchanged cycles the\n  required median is 64.94 MHz.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 16\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: |\n      Add registered three-bit one-hot near/far/saved operand selections\n      to ID/EX and a unified registered write_value field to MEM/WB.\n      Keep architectural, control and RVFI payload fields correct.\n  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n    description: |\n      Move dependency matching and newest-writer priority to decode.\n      Compare offered raw source fields with next EX/MEM and MEM/WB\n      destinations, using actual trap-adjusted next-state permissions.\n      Exclude x0 and emit one-hot selections for ID/EX capture.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Capture complete forwarding choices with the corresponding token\n      and RF operands. Preserve them across stage holds; annul invalid\n      tokens on reset/flush/bubbles. Maintain write-first reads and\n      simultaneous completion-cycle consumer capture.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Consume registered selections with parallel masked operand muxes,\n      removing execute-side tag comparison and permission qualification.\n      Expose the next EX/MEM producer's actual write permission after\n      alignment-trap adjustment, including blocking completions. Preserve\n      ALU, branch, M ownership and captured RVFI semantics.\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Register the selected extended-load-or-ALU writeback value before\n      WB, and expose the next MEM/WB producer's actual trap-adjusted write\n      permission for decode. Retain unified data and forwarding metadata\n      on dmem holds while clearing retirement validity. Preserve memory\n      masks, alignment handling, stable payload and RVFI captures.\n  - file: rtl/wb_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Drive w_data directly from the unified MEM/WB write_value register,\n      removing combinational ALU/load selection from both WB bypass paths.\n      Preserve valid-qualified RF writes, destination and x0 rules.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Wire decode-side producer identities/permissions and captured\n      selections, and connect the unified WB source. Preserve load-use,\n      dmem/M hold and recovery priorities, all top-level ports, nret=1\n      and the existing single retirement boundary.\n  - file: test/test_ex_stage.py\n    description: |\n      Adapt packed layouts and source selection stimuli to three-bit\n      one-hot inputs while preserving all existing arithmetic, branch,\n      ownership, backpressure and RVFI assertions. Verify actual write\n      permissions, trap cancellation and once-only M operand capture.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Cover adjacent ALU chains, equal-rd writers, trap-canceled writers\n      with older fallback, load-to-ALU/branch/store dependencies,\n      M-completion consumers, both-source forwarding and x0. Combine\n      long imem/dmem/M holds with retained WB data. Check exact sources,\n      results, contiguous order, no duplicate memory effects and progress.\n      Preserve all existing tests and run unchanged formal, stalled random\n      cosim, canonical CoreMark and median Gowin timing.\n'''\nprint('*** Begin Patch')\nprint('*** Update File: '+str(p.resolve()))\nprint('@@')\nfor line in p.read_text().splitlines():print('-'+line)\nfor line in new.splitlines():print('+'+line)\nprint('*** End Patch')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_1-sol_xhigh-v2-rep1/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260930-002-r6s1-hypgen/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-002-r6s1.yaml\n@@\n-id: hyp-20260930-002-r6s1\n-title: \"Retimed forwarding with decode-stage dependency matches\"\n-category: structural\n-motivation: |\n-  The champion scores 150.32 iterations/second at 62.085 MHz with\n-  4,130,235 bracketed CoreMark cycles. Its worst reported Gowin path\n-  starts at a MEM/WB destination-register bit, crosses forward_unit\n-  and execute, and ends in the fetch predictor. The previous structural\n-  flop-register-file attempt moved the limit to the same destination-tag\n-  forwarding network followed by the ALU and data-memory address path,\n-  reaching only 61.852 MHz at unchanged cycles. Registering IF/ID slowed\n-  CoreMark, and adding a complete operand stage failed stalled random\n-  cosim. Retiming dependency matching within the existing stages targets\n-  the common head of both remaining execution paths without adding an\n-  instruction latency or a new stage-wide backpressure protocol.\n-hypothesis: |\n-  Move register-number dependency comparisons out of the execute interval\n-  and into decode. For each offered instruction's rs1 and rs2, compare\n-  against the destination numbers currently in ID/EX and EX/MEM. Capture\n-  both potential-match bits per source alongside the existing ID/EX\n-  instruction. After a normal advancing edge these producers occupy\n-  EX/MEM and MEM/WB, respectively, so execute can select forwarding from\n-  registered matches and the producers' registered write permissions,\n-  rather than live five-bit comparisons and a priority encoder. This is\n-  one structural retiming of the bypass network; preserve the current\n-  banked distributed-RAM register file, pipeline depth, fetch skid buffer,\n-  predictor policy, blocking M units and nret=1 retirement interface.\n-\n-  Store potential matches, not an irrevocable priority choice. In execute\n-  qualify the near match with EX/MEM's actual nonzero\n…[16469 of 19541 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:4e90f21cbacc26d0]…\n+      dmem/M hold and recovery priorities, all top-level ports, nret=1\n+      and the existing single retirement boundary.\n+  - file: test/test_ex_stage.py\n+    description: |\n+      Adapt packed layouts and source selection stimuli to three-bit\n+      one-hot inputs while preserving all existing arithmetic, branch,\n+      ownership, backpressure and RVFI assertions. Verify actual write\n+      permissions, trap cancellation and once-only M operand capture.\n+  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n+    description: |\n+      Cover adjacent ALU chains, equal-rd writers, trap-canceled writers\n+      with older fallback, load-to-ALU/branch/store dependencies,\n+      M-completion consumers, both-source forwarding and x0. Combine\n+      long imem/dmem/M holds with retained WB data. Check exact sources,\n+      results, contiguous order, no duplicate memory effects and progress.\n+      Preserve all existing tests and run unchanged formal, stalled random\n+      cosim, canonical CoreMark and median Gowin timing.\n*** End Patch\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
