{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d.get('category')=='structural':\n  print(json.dumps({k:d.get(k) for k in ['id','title','outcome','fitness','fmax_mhz','cycles','critical_path','error']},indent=2))\n  h=d.get('hypothesis',{})\n  print('PROPOSAL:',h.get('hypothesis','') if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\n  print('NOTES:',d.get('implementation_notes',''))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20260929-002-r1s1\",\n  \"title\": \"Remove unrolled division from EX with a blocking iterative divider\",\n  \"outcome\": \"improvement\",\n  \"fitness\": 110.0,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 49.408,\n  \"cycles\": 4491817,\n  \"critical_path\": {\n    \"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s\",\n    \"to\": \"cpu/u_id/id_ex_w.rs2_val_0_s100\",\n    \"slack_ns\": -15.917,\n    \"arrival_ns\": 26.211,\n    \"logic_cells\": 36,\n    \"modules\": [\n      \"clock_ibuf\",\n      \"cpu/u_id\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex\",\n      \"cpu/u_if\",\n      \"cpu/u_hazard\",\n      \"cpu/u_id\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"error\": null\n}\nPROPOSAL: Make DIV, DIVU, REM and REMU blocking multicycle EX operations using one\nshared radix-2 restoring divider. Capture the post-forwarding operands\nand operation exactly once, register quotient/remainder state, and\nperform one 33-bit subtract/select step per cycle for 32 iterations.\nRegister sign correction and the final result before it returns to the\nordinary EX/MEM path. This removes every real combinational / and %\noperator from the synthesized ALU, while keeping RV32I and multiplication\nat their current latency.\n\nFreeze fetch and ID/EX while the divider owns EX, but let older EX/MEM\nand MEM/WB instructions drain. Insert invalid, side-effect-free EX/MEM\nbubbles while waiting; do not repeatedly hold and reissue an older\nmemory operation. Existing dmem backpressure still holds a pending older\nmemory request, and has priority over advancing EX/MEM. Accept a divide\nonly from a valid legal instruction when EX can start it; retain a\ncompleted result until downstream accepts it. On that acceptance edge,\nrelease ID/EX and transfer the captured instruction and operands with\nits result exactly once. Captured operands must not depend on forwarding\nsources remaining live after older instructions retire. Qualify redirects\nwith a valid instruction actually advancing, and cancel divider state on\nreset. Preserve the nret=1 interface, channel-0 retirement order and all\nexisting decoder, trap, memory and RVFI behavior.\n\nImplement signed division by unsigned magnitudes, restoring quotie\n…[34349 of 37421 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:2ee88aa6c023d0e3]…\ner's tied-high ready signals cannot exercise. This is not\na full formal pass. Complete all ordinary gates on the final RTL and\nadd directed stale-prediction plus memory-backpressure coverage during\nimplementation without modifying any contract file or weakening tests.\nThe main risks are recovery age/hold mistakes, a slow register proof,\nand placement variation. Acceptance requires (new_Fmax / 74.535) /\n(new_cycles / 4130235) > 1.046; at the measured cycle count the median\nmust exceed 79.165 MHz. Predict 6 percent with medium confidence.\n\nThe C++ cosim harness has separate instruction and data memories, so\na self-modifying ELF cannot create the required stale-prediction\nload/store corner there. Exercise that corner in cocotb by changing\nthe instruction delivered by the imem model after training a PC, while\nretaining the predictor state. The existing eight trace cases passed\non the final scratch RTL; this additional directed corner is still a\nrequired implementation test, not a claimed prototype pass.\n\nNOTES: \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
