{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_77", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-002-r8s1.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20260930-002-r8s1\ntitle: \"Carry-select arithmetic across the existing execute-result boundary\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 192.51 iterations/second at 80.738 MHz and\n  4,193,876 bracketed CoreMark cycles. Its reported worst Gowin path\n  starts at ID/EX.rs1_val and ends at EX/MEM.alu_result through the ALU,\n  taking 19.233 ns across fourteen cells. Complete registered bypass\n  choices and separate registered memory/recovery lanes have removed\n  earlier control and memory-endpoint limits. The remaining integer\n  result path still combines operand selection, full-width arithmetic\n  and late result selection before one register edge. Earlier attempts\n  to add a general operand stage failed stalled cosim, and result-mask\n  predecode alone did not improve median timing. Split arithmetic work\n  across the existing result boundary while retaining instruction latency.\nhypothesis: |\n  Represent ADD, ADDI, SUB and AUIPC results in EX/MEM as registered\n  carry-select components instead of requiring a completed 32-bit sum\n  before that edge. This is one structural repartition of integer\n  arithmetic and its bypass representation. Compute the low sixteen-bit\n  sum and carry, plus two upper sixteen-bit sums for assumed carry zero\n  and one, in parallel from the existing forwarded ALU operands. Register\n  the low result, carry and both upper candidates at the current EX/MEM\n  boundary. In the following cycle choose the upper candidate with the\n  registered carry and concatenate it with the registered low result.\n  The longest carry propagation before EX/MEM is then sixteen bits.\n\n  For SUB use a + ~b + 1, injecting one into the low slice and using\n  the same two upper carry candidates. All sums are modulo 2^32 with\n  explicit widths; sign extension and AUIPC's PC operand stay exact.\n  Use an operation-qualified arithmetic representation bit captured\n  with the token. Keep a separate registered plain result for logical,\n  compare, shift, LUI, jump-link and completed M instructions. Their\n  cur\n…[5344 of 8416 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:dee60f0c412d99ed]…\ntructed modulo-2^32 ADD/SUB,\n      including sixteen-bit carry boundaries, wraparound and signed\n      extremes. Preserve all real M-result and backpressure checks.\n  - file: test/test_ex_stage.py\n    description: |\n      Adapt packed EX/MEM layout assertions and verify reconstructed\n      arithmetic, plain/link/M selection, held components, bubbles,\n      reset and pending recovery without dropping existing checks.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Verify adjacent ADD/SUB chains, both-source forwarding, repeated\n      same-rd writers, x0, AUIPC and carry/borrow propagation across bit\n      sixteen. Include load/M producers and arithmetic results consumed\n      by branches, JALR, loads and stores under combined imem/dmem holds.\n      Preserve exact RVFI/order and once-only memory assertions. Run\n      unchanged formal, trace cosim, canonical CoreMark validation and\n      Gowin median timing before accepting an implementation.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
