hat acceptance edge,\nrelease ID/EX and transfer the captured instruction and operands with\nits result exactly once. Captured operands must not depend on forwarding\nsources remaining live after older instructions retire. Qualify redirects\nwith a valid instruction actually advancing, and cancel divider state on\nreset. Preserve the nret=1 interface, channel-0 retirement order and all\nexisting decoder, trap, memory and RVFI behavior.\n\nImplement signed division by unsigned magnitudes, restoring quotient sign\nfrom the operand-sign XOR and remainder sign from the dividend. Preserve\ntruncation toward zero, quotient\n…[13710 of 16782 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:7bd494232454cea9]…\n near forwarding.\n\nExpose an internal fast_out from alu containing exactly the ordinary\nADD/SUB, logic, compare, shift and LUI results; its M/default arms are\nzero. Keep the original out behavior for direct ALU users and tests by\nselecting the existing dedicated mul_result/div_result ports for M\noperations and fast_out for ordinary operations. Execute consumes\nfast_out rather than the all-operation out, so its ordinary path has\nno redundant selection of M results inside the ALU. JAL/JALR retain\ntheir existing PC+4 override in the ordinary lane. Leave every real\nRV32M algorithm, correction step, ALTOPS formula and handshake intact.\n\nDefine D = div_owned_q && div_result_valid and\nM = mul_owned_q && mul_result_valid, using the existing mutually\nexclusive ownership state. On each nonreset, nonstalled edge capture\nresult_payload = ({32{!D && !M}} & fast_instruction.alu_result) |\n                 ({32{D}} & div_result) |\n                 ({32{M}} & mul_result).\nThe result register must not depend on redirect, ex_w\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
