d-use holds, dmem stalls and blocking M execution.\n  A skid token uses its captured predicted_next_pc, never a new table lookup.\n  Narrow validity/side-effect kills still cancel wrong-path instructions.\n  Preserve all nret=1 ports, decode legality, real/ALTOPS M arithmetic,\n  memory protocol, contiguous RVFI order and bounded forward progress.\n\n  The intended CoreMark cycle count is unchanged from 4,193,876 under the\n  standard independent bus stalls. The success condition is measured\n  median Gowin Fmax above 98.018568 MHz if cycles are identical, giving\n  fitness more than 4.6 percent above 223.44. Expect roughly eight percent\n  fitness improvement from shortening recovery and static alignment\n  paths. Main risks are a new ID immediate-add/subtract/comparison path\n  becoming critical and extra ID/EX registers affecting placement; this\n  estimate needs implementation and vendor median verification. Keep all\n  formal/cosim, canonical CRCs, validation literal, marker-only timing and\n  out-of-bounds gates intact; do not alter any evaluator or contract file.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: |\n      Extend id_ex_t with static_control_target, registered sequential\n      and static prediction mismatch bits, and the two full-width JALR\n      inverse-base candidates. Preserve predicted_next_pc and RVFI metadata.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Prepare static target, both static successor mismatch bits and\n      modular JALR inverse candidates from the offered token and decoded\n      immediate. Capture them on the existing payload enable, with exact\n      hold/flush ownership and no extra pipeline stage or live table lookup.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Use the registered static target for branch/JAL resolution and\n      registered successor mismatch bits for recovery. Replace JALR\n      sum-to-predicted-PC comparison wit