{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"agent_message","text":"Both direct decode-calculation prototypes failed timing; the first preserved CoreMark cycles and passed CRC validation. The final hypothesis instead stores comparison signatures alongside BTB targets, letting decode carry the checks without doing target arithmetic. Its fitness gain remains an estimate."}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_43", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-003-r10s2.yaml')\np.write_text('''id: hyp-20260930-003-r10s2\ntitle: \\\"Cache successor comparison signatures alongside predicted targets\\\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Prediction recovery remains a timing limit after the champion's operand\n  and shifter improvements. The r9s2 worst path ran from MEM/WB forwarded\n  data to EX redirect through 31 cells, and r9s1 also exposed forwarding\n  to recovery timing. A canonical CoreMark ISS profile found only 1,194\n  ideal changing-return-target errors, insufficient headroom for a return\n  stack alone. Scratch prototypes moving target/inverse calculations\n  directly into ID preserved 4,193,876 CoreMark cycles and canonical CRCs,\n  but reduced median Gowin Fmax to 78.978 MHz, or 67.343 MHz with RAM16\n  banking. Their critical path became BTB lookup followed by inverse\n  arithmetic into ID/EX. This identifies the better predictor angle:\n  cache comparison operands during resolved training, so neither EX\n  forwarding nor the current fetch lookup feeds a serial carry chain\n  before prediction validation.\nhypothesis: |\n  Augment the existing tagged 64-entry next-PC predictor with successor\n  comparison signatures. Preserve its two-bit direction policy, capacity,\n  fall-through skid, pipeline depth and EX/MEM-owned registered recovery.\n  A predicted target and its signature form one immutable accepted-fetch\n  token. Decode prepares only equality/validity bits from cached metadata;\n  it must not subtract the live predicted PC or compute a full static\n  target followed by equality on the fetch-to-ID/EX path.\n\n  For each allocated entry store its control kind (PC-relative branch/JAL\n  or JALR), whether its target equals that entry PC+4, and the PC-relative\n  displacement for branch/JAL entries. JALR entries additionally store\n  their signed 12-bit immediate and two full-width inverse rs1 candidates.\n  Extend resolved feedback with control kind, decoded displacement,\n  JALR immediate and the actual forwarded rs1. Generate signatures only\n  from this existing registered once-per-advance feedback. For a JALR\n  let s = resolved_rs1[0] XOR immediate[0]. Its two candidates are\n  resolved_rs1 - s and resolved_rs1 + (1-s), modulo 2\"'^32. These equal\n  resolved_target - immediate and resolved_target + 1 - immediate because\n  JALR clears the sum'\"'s bit zero. The training lane therefore needs only\n  conditional increment/decrement, never a forwarding-to-wide-subtract\n  bypass into prediction. Calculate target-equals-PC+4 from registered\n  feedback. Write target, kind and signature together on allocation.\n\n  On a predicted-taken tagged hit capture the exact selected entry's\n  signature with predicted_next_pc. On miss or predicted-not-taken capture\n  a sequential signature: displacement 4, sequential-match true and no\n  usable JALR inverse signature. The skid retains every metadata field\n  with its instruction and PC. In ID compute static-target mismatch as\n  cached displacement \"'!= decoded immediate when the signature describes\n  a PC-relative successor; a JALR-kind signature conservatively mismatches\n  a static target. Sequential mismatch is the negation of the captured\n  exact target-equals-PC+4 flag. Register these narrow decisions in ID/EX,\n  together with the cached inverse candidates and a JALR-signature-usable\n  bit requiring a predicted JALR kind and an exact immediate match.\n\n  EX selects registered sequential/static mismatch with the resolved\n  outcome. For a usable JALR signature, compare the actual forwarded rs1\n  against both cached candidates in parallel. A match requires either\n  equality and predicted_next_pc[0]==0. This is exact for the captured\n  target, including odd bases, negative offsets and 32-bit wraparound.\n  If the signature kind or immediate does not match, or a sequential\n  prediction has no inverse signature, conservatively request recovery\n  to the actual architectural target even if the predicted PC happens\n  to equal it. This extra flush is safe and must be documented; never\n  accept an unverifiable prediction or reintroduce the full sum-to-PC\n  comparator as a fallback. Such cases primarily accompany BTB misses\n  or changed instructions. Keep actual JALR rs1+imm and branch/JAL PC+imm\n  adders in EX for architectural pc_next and redirect_target, in parallel\n  with these comparisons. No target arithmetic is moved into ID.\n\n  Physically bank all BTB payload into four constant-index RAM16 banks:\n  bank PC[7:6], word PC[5:2], full tag PC[31:8]. Resolve each bank'\"'s tag,\n  validity and direction locally before masked-OR target and signature\n  selection. Use asynchronous reads, synchronous bank-local writes and\n  distributed_ram attributes, resetting validity only. Keep independent\n  update-hit reads as needed for RAM inference. This supports the wider\n  signature table without BSRAM output-to-decode arithmetic; it is part\n  of this single predictor organization, with no replay or fetch FIFO.\n  Verify actual Gowin RAM16 mapping. Lookup observes the pre-edge entry\n  on simultaneous training, with no same-cycle feedback bypass.\n\n  Preserve exact tag validation and stale-entry invalidation for ordinary,\n  illegal and misaligned resolutions. A changed JALR immediate invalidates\n  usability of old inverse candidates even if the BTB tag still matches.\n  Hold all captured fields under original ID/EX and skid enables. Keep\n  alignment traps, untaken-misaligned-branch behavior, jump link writes,\n  one-shot training, retained older recovery through dmem stalls, younger\n  store/M-request squash, arithmetic and nret=1 RVFI order unchanged.\n  Never assume predicted control kind establishes decoder legality.\n\n  The final cached-signature architecture has not been synthesized; the\n  failed direct-calculation prototypes establish its timing constraints,\n  not an improvement claim. Expect about eight percent fitness gain from\n  removing prediction-check carry chains while retaining normal latency.\n  With unchanged 4,193,876 bracketed cycles, median Fmax must exceed\n  98.018568 MHz to clear 4.6 percent above the 223.44 champion. Measure\n  actual cycles because conservative unverifiable-JALR recovery can add\n  bubbles. Principal risks are wider lookup routing, conditional increment\n  training paths and remaining forwarding-to-trap/bypass paths limiting\n  Fmax. Require the normal formal/cosim gates, canonical CRCs and validation\n  literal, independent bus stalls, marker-only timing, OOB checks and\n  median across all Gowin placement options. No contract changes.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: |\n      Extend predictor_update_t with control kind, static displacement,\n      JALR immediate and resolved forwarded rs1. Extend if_id_t with the\n      captured signature and id_ex_t with prepared mismatch/usability bits\n      and inverse candidates. Keep predicted_next_pc and RVFI metadata.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Emit signature-training inputs in existing registered advancing\n      feedback. Use registered sequential/static checks and parallel\n      forwarded-rs1 inverse equality for usable JALR signatures, otherwise\n      recover conservatively to the actual target. Preserve actual target\n      adders, alignment traps, architectural successor/link data, recovery\n      ownership and all existing stall/squash priorities.\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Store coherent target/signature payload in four RAM16 banks with\n      bank-local tagged direction decisions and masked-OR selection.\n      Generate signature payload solely from registered resolved feedback,\n      includin