{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_16", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n r=json.loads(line)\n if r['id'] in ('hyp-20260930-003-r9s2','hyp-20260930-001-r9s0'):\n  print(r['id'])\n  print(json.dumps({k:r.get(k) for k in ('cycles','fmax_mhz','critical_path','lutram','bsram')},indent=2))\n  print(r.get('motivation'))\n  print(r.get('hypothesis',{}).get('hypothesis'))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20260930-001-r9s0\n{\n  \"cycles\": 4193876,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 93.708,\n  \"critical_path\": {\n    \"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.write_value_14_s0\",\n    \"to\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.fwd_rs2_sel_1_s0\",\n    \"slack_ns\": -5.763,\n    \"arrival_ns\": 16.058,\n    \"logic_cells\": 25,\n    \"modules\": [\n      \"clock_ibuf\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex\",\n      \"cpu/u_fwd\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"lutram\": 32,\n  \"bsram\": 7\n}\nThe champion scores 209.45 at 87.839 MHz and 4,193,876 bracketed\nCoreMark cycles. Its worst Gowin path runs from EX/MEM.alu_result[27]\nto EX/MEM.alu_result[7] through the ALU in 16.702 ns across twelve\ncells. Accepted operand preselection has removed serial forwarding\ndecisions, leaving ordinary ALU implementation as a timing opportunity.\nExisting SLL/SRL/SRA use separate dynamic shift expressions. Prior\nmicro_opt history supports shortening combinational paths at unchanged\ninstruction cycles; the sibling result-ownership partition did not\nbeat the current champion. A local grouped shifter is a distinct angle.\n\nReplace only ordinary shift implementation in alu.sv with explicit\nradix-4 grouped barrel networks. Keep the binary operation encoding,\nexisting ALU ports, complete registered operand selections, pipeline\nboundaries and instruction latencies unchanged. There is no additional\nregister, stall, prediction policy or execution stage.\n\nBuild separate left and right data networks, each with three steps.\nDecode b[1:0] into low_sel = 4'b0001 << b[1:0] and b[3:2] into\nmid_sel = 4'b0001 << b[3:2]. The first step selects shifts of 0/1/2/3\nbits; the second selects 0/4/8/12 bits; the final step selects 0/16\nbits using b[4]. Express each four-way step as an OR of four data\nterms masked by the mutually exclusive selector bits. Use fixed slices\nand concatenations rather than variable shift expressions inside the\nnetwork. Left shifts always fill zero. Both SRL and SRA share the\nright network, with fill = (op == ALU_SRA) && a[31]; each fixed right\nshift concatenates the required number of copies of this original fill\nbit. Right fill remains correct through both \n…[11036 of 14108 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:eebeb190e4de8057]…\n exact\ncaptured predictions through stalls, and resolution of every valid\ninstruction against its architectural successor. Keep the champion's\ncomplete ALU operand choices, blocking M arithmetic, decoder default\nlegality, alignment traps, bus protocol and nret=1 RVFI contract.\n\nThe prototype's cycle count includes registered-queue refill and\nrecovery latency. At 3,868,725 cycles, exceeding the champion by the\nrequired 4.6 percent needs median Fmax above 84.758 MHz. Its measured\n87.662 MHz clears that threshold, supporting an eight percent expected\nfitness gain with medium confidence. Prototype evidence is not an\naccepted tournament result. The principal risks are formal correctness\nin FIFO/replay invalidation corners and implementation drift that\nrestores tag-before-comparison selection or fetch/hazard feedback.\nVerify actual RAM mapping, all unchanged formal/cosim gates,\ncanonical CoreMark CRCs and validation literal with both standard bus\nstalls, marker-only cycles, OOB checks and all-option Gowin median.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
