{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_38", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n r=json.loads(line)\n if r['id']=='hyp-20260930-003-r10s2':\n  print(r['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Augment the existing tagged 64-entry next-PC predictor with successor\ncomparison signatures. Preserve its two-bit direction policy, capacity,\nfall-through skid, pipeline depth and EX/MEM-owned registered recovery.\nA predicted target and its signature form one immutable accepted-fetch\ntoken. Decode prepares only equality/validity bits from cached metadata;\nit must not subtract the live predicted PC or compute a full static\ntarget followed by equality on the fetch-to-ID/EX path.\n\nFor each allocated entry store its control kind (PC-relative branch/JAL\nor JALR), whether its target equals that entry PC+4, and the PC-relative\ndisplacement for branch/JAL entries. JALR entries additionally store\ntheir signed 12-bit immediate and two full-width inverse rs1 candidates.\nExtend resolved feedback with control kind, decoded displacement,\nJALR immediate and the actual forwarded rs1. Generate signatures only\nfrom this existing registered once-per-advance feedback. For a JALR\nlet s = resolved_rs1[0] XOR immediate[0]. Its two candidates are\nresolved_rs1 - s and resolved_rs1 + (1-s), modulo 2^32. These equal\nresolved_target - immediate and resolved_target + 1 - immediate because\nJALR clears the sum's bit zero. The training lane therefore needs only\nconditional increment/decrement, never a forwarding-to-wide-subtract\nbypass into prediction. Calculate target-equals-PC+4 from registered\nfeedback. Write target, kind and signature together on allocation.\n\nOn a predicted-taken tagged hit capture the exact selected entry's\nsignature with predicted_next_pc. On miss or predicted-not-taken capture\na sequential signature: displacement 4, sequential-match true and no\nusable JALR inverse signature. The skid retains every metadata field\nwith its instruction and PC. In ID compute static-target mismatch as\ncached displacement != decoded immediate when the signature describes\na PC-relative successor; a JALR-kind signature conservatively mismatches\na static target. Sequential mismatch is the negation of the captured\nexact target-equals-PC+4 flag. Re\n…[2212 of 5284 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:1a1bdab50c176dd4]…\nned older recovery through dmem stalls, younger\nstore/M-request squash, arithmetic and nret=1 RVFI order unchanged.\nNever assume predicted control kind establishes decoder legality.\n\nThe final cached-signature architecture has not been synthesized; the\nfailed direct-calculation prototypes establish its timing constraints,\nnot an improvement claim. Expect about eight percent fitness gain from\nremoving prediction-check carry chains while retaining normal latency.\nWith unchanged 4,193,876 bracketed cycles, median Fmax must exceed\n98.018568 MHz to clear 4.6 percent above the 223.44 champion. Measure\nactual cycles because conservative unverifiable-JALR recovery can add\nbubbles. Principal risks are wider lookup routing, conditional increment\ntraining paths and remaining forwarding-to-trap/bypass paths limiting\nFmax. Require the normal formal/cosim gates, canonical CRCs and validation\nliteral, independent bus stalls, marker-only timing, OOB checks and\nmedian across all Gowin placement options. No contract changes.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
