{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_11", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n    r=json.loads(line)\n    if r['id'] in ('hyp-20260930-003-r9s2','hyp-20260930-003-r10s2','hyp-20260930-003-r11s2'):\n        h=r.get('hypothesis',{})\n        print('\\\\n',r['id'])\n        print(h.get('motivation',r.get('motivation')) if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\n        if isinstance(h,dict):print(h.get('hypothesis'))\n        print('PATH',r.get('critical_path'))\n        print('NOTES',r.get('implementation_notes'))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "\n hyp-20260930-003-r9s2\nThe champion scores 209.45 iterations/second at 87.839 MHz over\n4,193,876 marker-bracketed CoreMark cycles. Its existing 64-entry\nnext-PC predictor already captures most branch-direction benefit:\nearlier architectural modeling found only 4,384 fewer errors when\nincreasing the table to 128 entries. Instruction stream replay has\nsubstantially more measured headroom under the contracted bus stalls.\n\nThe last predictor attempt, hyp-20260930-003-r8s2, passed formal and\ncosim and reduced the marker interval to 3,868,195 cycles by combining\neight branch-discovered replay blocks with a registered two-token\nfrontend. Its 78.941 MHz median made fitness only 204.08. The reported\nworst path was fetch PC to the BTB tag memory, with 31 logic cells;\nthe earlier fall-through replay attempt instead exposed a replay-hit\nthrough hazard backpressure to replay address-register path. These\nresults identify a frontend implementation bottleneck rather than\ninsufficient replay coverage. Explicit RAM16 banking has already\nimproved the register file on this FPGA. Apply that storage discipline\nto predictor lookup while retaining a registered replay-to-ID boundary.\n\nA scratch prototype on the exact champion confirms why banking alone\nis insufficient: selecting a bank's full tag before comparing it gave\nonly 80.412 MHz median. Comparing tag, validity and direction locally\nwithin each bank, then combining masked target words, gave vendor\nplacement-option Fmax values of 78.893/87.662/87.662 MHz. Its median is\n87.662 MHz and its standard stalled CoreMark interval is 3,868,725\ncycles, yielding 226.59 iterations/second, 8.18 percent above 209.45.\nAll five canonical CRCs, the validation literal, EBREAK completion\nand the OOB check pass. Selftest and all three random-program RVFI\ncosim comparisons also pass with both bus stalls. Area is 6,075 LUT4,\n1,782 FF, 176 LUTRAM, four BSRAM and two DSP. Full formal has not been\nrun on this scratch variant; historical r8s2 passing formal does not\nestablish a formal pass for this proposa\n…[16205 of 19277 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:a8dc2f307fda7753]…\next, and nret=1 retirement\norder. This is one predictor-verification change, with no replay cache,\nnew fetch stage, signature arithmetic, or predictor-accuracy changes.\n\nExpected gain is approximately seven percent from higher Fmax with\nunchanged architectural execution and recovery cycles. This is an\nunmeasured estimate. At unchanged 4,193,876 cycles, acceptance needs\nmedian Gowin Fmax above 98.018568 MHz. The main risks are comparison\nfanout into IF/ID controls, the successor-select capture path, and the\nchampion's separate forwarding-permission path becoming dominant.\nRequire existing unit/formal/cosim gates, canonical CoreMark CRCs and\nvalidation literal, marker-only cycles, OOB checks, independent bus\nstalls, and median vendor timing. Do not modify any evaluation contract.\n\nPATH {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/reg_q.pc_next_2_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_if/tags_tags_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -8.861, 'arrival_ns': 19.155, 'logic_cells': 39, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_if', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_if']}\nNOTES \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
