{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_4", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n '\\\"category\\\": ?\\\"predictor\\\"|hyp-20260930-003-r12s2|hyp-20260930-003-r13s2|hyp-20260930-003-r10s2|hyp-20260930-003-r11s2' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "4:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260929-003-r1s2\", \"title\": \"64-entry tagged next-PC predictor with two-bit branch direction\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The baseline fetches sequentially and flushes the combinational IF/ID\\ninstruction whenever EX resolves a taken branch or jump. Because IF/ID\\nis not registered, each such transfer loses one fetch/decode opportunity,\\nrather than the two bubbles suggested by the five-stage comments.\\nCoreMark repeatedly executes loop branches and call sites, making these\\nbubbles a promising source of cycle savings. The measured 199.837 ns\\ncritical path is through forwarding and the combinational ALU; a small\\nPC-indexed predictor should improve iterations/cycle without adding\\nlogic to that arithmetic path. No predictor experiments or lessons are\\npresent in this fixture's history.\\n\\nA fresh architectural trace of the canonical -O3, RV32IM, 2K,\\nten-iteration CoreMark ELF contains 2,922,016 bracketed instructions,\\n529,588 conditional branches, 49,367 JALs, and 13,735 JALRs. Sequential\\nprediction would mispredict 357,527 next PCs. A 64-entry tagged table\\nwith this policy reduces next-PC errors to 62,551; 32 entries give\\n73,619 errors and 128 entries give 58,167. Thus 64 entries capture most\\nof the available benefit without doubling storage for only 4,384 fewer\\nerrors. This trace model uses immediate training and no speculative\\npipeline or bus timing, so it supports the sizing decision rather than\\nconstituting a measured RTL speedup.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The baseline fetches sequentially and flushes the combinational IF/ID\\ninstruction whenever EX resolves a taken branch or jump. Because IF/ID\\nis not registered, each such transfer loses one fetch/decode opportunity,\\nrather than the two bubbles suggested by the five-stage comments.\\nCoreMark repeatedly executes loop branches and call sites, making these\\nbubbles a promising source of cycle savings. The measured 199.837 ns\\ncritical path is through forwarding and the combinational ALU; a small\\nPC-indexed predi\n…[157575 of 160647 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:fb456318f66d61db]…\nin pipeline checks and exercise forwarded JALR operands, changing\\nindirect targets, taken/not-taken loops, stale ordinary/illegal/M\\npredictions, full-skid recovery and both bus stalls. Check exact RVFI\\nPCs/order/traps/link writes and no younger register/store/M effects.\\n\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 220.65, \"delta_pct\": -1.25, \"vs_baseline\": 1720.54, \"fmax_mhz\": 92.538, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4193876, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3752, \"ff\": 1188, \"seeds\": [87.884, 92.538, 92.538], \"perturbations\": [[0, 87.884, 12], [1, 92.538, 10], [2, 92.538, 10]], \"lutram\": 32, \"bsram\": 7, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.alu_b_sel_2_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result_5_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -6.379, \"arrival_ns\": 16.673, \"logic_cells\": 13, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 12, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-30T10:36:32.927498Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 13}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
