{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d.get('category')=='predictor' and d['id'] in ['hyp-20260930-003-r9s2','hyp-20260930-003-r10s2','hyp-20260930-003-r11s2']:\n  print(d['id'])\n  h=d.get('hypothesis')\n  print(h.get('hypothesis') if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\n  print(d.get('implementation_notes',''))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20260930-003-r9s2\nImplement one instruction stream predictor: retain previously fetched\nwords in eight tagged 64-byte blocks discovered by resolved backward\nbranches, and replay them when the instruction bus is unavailable.\nUse the proven registered two-token fetch topology from r8s2, but\nexplicitly bank the associated 64-entry next-PC table into four\nindependent 16-entry asynchronous-read distributed-RAM banks with\nbank-local prediction decisions. The local decisions are essential:\nbanking followed by a wide tag mux missed the acceptance clock in\nthe scratch experiment. Keep the established prediction algorithm\nand table capacity.\n\nSplit BTB tags and targets by PC[7:6], with PC[5:2] addressing each\nRAM16 bank. Retain full PC[31:8] tags, target[31:2], unconditional\nbits, valid bits and saturating two-bit counters. Declare payload\nmemories inside constant-index generate banks with distributed_ram\nattributes, asynchronous reads and bank-local synchronous writes.\nReset only validity. In each constant bank independently compare its\nasynchronous tag read against fetch PC[31:8] and combine equality,\nentry validity, PC[7:6] matching that bank, and unconditional/counter\ndirection to produce a one-bit predict_bank signal. Mask that bank's\n30-bit target with predict_bank and OR all four targets; select this\nresult versus PC+4 with the OR of predict_bank. Do not select a wide\ntag or wide counter/target tuple before performing the tag comparison.\nThe implementation must preserve the locally resolved decision before\ntarget selection, rather than merely adding distributed_ram hints.\nPreserve a pre-edge lookup on concurrent training, including identical-index\nlookup/update. Give update-hit detection its own asynchronous tag and\ncounter read view if inference requires replication; do not serialize\ntraining through the prediction read or add a live training bypass.\nCheck the vendor synthesis report actually maps these payload arrays\nto RAM16 rather than BSRAM. Do not introduce a pipeline cycle into\nthe next-PC recurrence or a\n…[12103 of 15175 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:88ff18856e3bb973]…\naining exactly as the previous redirect did. Preserve\nfull-tag allocation, matching-only stale-entry invalidation, legal\naligned control allocation, counter saturation, pre-edge table lookup,\njump link writes, RVFI architectural pc_next, and nret=1 retirement\norder. This is one predictor-verification change, with no replay cache,\nnew fetch stage, signature arithmetic, or predictor-accuracy changes.\n\nExpected gain is approximately seven percent from higher Fmax with\nunchanged architectural execution and recovery cycles. This is an\nunmeasured estimate. At unchanged 4,193,876 cycles, acceptance needs\nmedian Gowin Fmax above 98.018568 MHz. The main risks are comparison\nfanout into IF/ID controls, the successor-select capture path, and the\nchampion's separate forwarding-permission path becoming dominant.\nRequire existing unit/formal/cosim gates, canonical CoreMark CRCs and\nvalidation literal, marker-only cycles, OOB checks, independent bus\nstalls, and median vendor timing. Do not modify any evaluation contract.\n\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
