{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg --files cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses cores/bench/test cores/bench/rtl && sed -n '1,240p' cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv && rg -n 'predict|trace|coremark|sim' Makefile tools/eval/fpga.py\"", "aggregated_output": "cores/bench/rtl/decoder.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/forward_unit.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/imm_gen.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/alu.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/reg_file.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/wb_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/core.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv\ncores/bench/test/test_imm_gen.py\ncores/bench/test/conftest.py\ncores/bench/test/test_mem_stage.py\ncores/bench/test/test_ex_stage.py\ncores/bench/test/test_if_stage.py\ncores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\ncores/bench/test/_helpers.py\ncores/bench/test/test_decoder.py\ncores/bench/test/test_reg_file.py\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py\n// rtl/if_stage.sv\n//\n// Instruction fetch stage. A one-entry fall-through skid buffer captures\n// ready fetches while ID is held. The empty-buffer path remains combinational\n// so ID/EX can accept the current fetch without an extra pipeline cycle.\n//\n// The tagged next-PC table reads only the registered fetch PC.\n// Each queued token retains the exact prediction used to advance fetch.\n// Recovery cancels the queue; ID kills validity and side effects rather than\n// putting recovery on the decode data path.\n//\n// Latency:        PC-reg update is synchronous; output is combinational.\n// RVFI fields:    feeds pc_rdata (via ID/EX/MEM/WB) and pc_wdata (via\n//                 EX-stage redirect).\nmodule if_stage (\n  input  logic              clock,\n  input  logic              reset,\n  input  logic              stall,            // offered ID token backpressure\n  input  logic              imem_ready,\n  input  logic              redirect,         // pending EX/MEM recovery\n  input  logic [31:0]       redirect_target,\n  input  predictor_update_t update,\n  output logic [31:0]       imem_addr,\n  input  logic [31:0]       imem_data,\n  output if_id_t  out\n);\n\n  localparam logic [31:0] RESET_PC = 32'h0000_0000;\n\n  logic [31:0] pc;\n  logic [31:0] predicted_next_pc;\n  logic [63:0] valid_q;\n  logic [23:0] tags [0:63];\n  logic [29:0] targets [0:63];\n  logic un\n…[6509 of 9581 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:c6969c10bbe6ea53]…\n\"\nMakefile:84:\t@echo \"  make bench              — build selftest + coremark ELFs\"\nMakefile:112:cosim: cosim-build bench/programs/selftest.elf bench/programs/coremark.elf\nMakefile:113:\tpython3 -m tools.eval.cosim . $(TARGET)\nMakefile:115:cosim-build: $(wildcard $(RTL_DIR)/*.sv) test/cosim/main.cpp\nMakefile:116:\tbash test/cosim/build.sh\nMakefile:137:fpga: cosim-build bench/programs/coremark.elf\nMakefile:143:bench/programs/coremark.elf: bench/programs/Makefile bench/programs/crt0.S \\\nMakefile:144:                              $(wildcard bench/programs/coremark/*.c) \\\nMakefile:145:                              $(wildcard bench/programs/coremark/*.h) \\\nMakefile:146:                              $(wildcard bench/programs/coremark/baremetal/*.c) \\\nMakefile:147:                              $(wildcard bench/programs/coremark/baremetal/*.h)\nMakefile:148:\t$(MAKE) -f bench/programs/Makefile bench/programs/coremark.elf\nMakefile:178:\trm -rf test/cosim/sim_build sim_build out\nMakefile:187:\trm -rf cores/$(TARGET)/sim_build\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d.get('category') \"'!= '\"'predictor': continue\n print('\\\\nID',d['id'],d['title'])\n for k in ('outcome','delta_pct','fitness','fmax_mhz','cycles','critical_path','error'): print(k, d.get(k))\n h=d.get('hypothesis',{})\n if isinstance(h,dict):\n  print('MOTIVATION', h.get('motivation',''))\n  print('PROPOSAL',h.get('hypothesis','')[:5500])\n print('NOTES', d.get('implementation_notes','')[:8000])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d.get('category') \"'!= '\"'predictor': continue\n print('\\\\nID',d['id'],d['title'])\n for k in ('outcome','delta_pct','fitness','fmax_mhz','cycles','critical_path','error'): print(k, d.get(k))\n h=d.get('hypothesis',{})\n if isinstance(h,dict):\n  print('MOTIVATION', h.get('motivation',''))\n  print('PROPOSAL',h.get('hypothesis','')[:5500])\n print('NOTES', d.get('implementation_notes','')[:8000])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "\nID hyp-20260929-003-r1s2 64-entry tagged next-PC predictor with two-bit branch direction\noutcome regression\ndelta_pct 7.84\nfitness 13.07\nfmax_mhz 5.487\ncycles 4197517\ncritical_path {'from': 'cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_1_s0', 'to': 'dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -189.85, 'arrival_ns': 200.144, 'logic_cells': 152, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_fwd', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\nerror None\nMOTIVATION The baseline fetches sequentially and flushes the combinational IF/ID\ninstruction whenever EX resolves a taken branch or jump. Because IF/ID\nis not registered, each such transfer loses one fetch/decode opportunity,\nrather than the two bubbles suggested by the five-stage comments.\nCoreMark repeatedly executes loop branches and call sites, making these\nbubbles a promising source of cycle savings. The measured 199.837 ns\ncritical path is through forwarding and the combinational ALU; a small\nPC-indexed predictor should improve iterations/cycle without adding\nlogic to that arithmetic path. No predictor experiments or lessons are\npresent in this fixture's history.\n\nA fresh architectural trace of the canonical -O3, RV32IM, 2K,\nten-iteration CoreMark ELF contains 2,922,016 bracketed instructions,\n529,588 conditional branches, 49,367 JALs, and 13,735 JALRs. Sequential\nprediction would mispredict 357,527 next PCs. A 64-entry tagged table\nwith this policy reduces next-PC errors to 62,551; 32 entries give\n73,619 errors and 128 entries give 58,167. Thus 64 entries capture most\nof the available benefit without doubling storage for only 4,384 fewer\nerrors. This trace model uses immediate training and no speculative\npipeline or bus timing, so it supports the sizing decision rather than\nconstituting a measured RTL speedup.\n\nPROPOSAL Add one 64-entry direct-mapped tagged branch-target buffer in if_stage.\nIndex with fetch PC[7:2]; each entry holds a valid bit, PC[31:8] tag,\naligned 30-bit target, unconditional-transfer bit, and a two-bit\nsaturating conditional-branch counter. Reset valid bits only, keeping\npayload arrays fre\n…[82370 of 85442 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:79787e7e84fb9052]…\nequality and bit-zero-\ncleared JALR sum equality with a standalone combinational SAT miter.\nRetain existing tests and exercise every segment boundary, long carries,\noverflow, negative offsets, all-zero/all-one operands, arbitrary\npredicted-bit errors and odd/even equivalent JALR bases. Require all\nunchanged formal/cosim gates and canonical stalled CoreMark CRCs,\nvalidation literal, bounds, marker-only cycles and median Gowin timing.\n\nExpect six percent fitness improvement with low confidence through\nshorter predictor verification, at exactly unchanged CoreMark cycles.\nAcceptance needs median Fmax above approximately 98.02 MHz. Unlike the\nprior bitwise verifier, this proposal deliberately retains short local\narithmetic carries and leaves the sequential comparator untouched.\nRisks are short-adder mapping, reduction routing, duplicated logic\nbeside the actual target adders and another execute path remaining\ndominant. Scratch timing is evidence about mapping, not a formal or\ntournament improvement claim.\n\nNOTES \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
