ity\nand data selection from decode hazards while retaining the measured\ninstruction-stall savings. This is one stream-predictor hypothesis;\nchanges to frontend buffering serve that predictor's timing boundary.\n\nA scratch prototype on the exact current champion uses 3,868,725\nbracketed cycles with both standard pseudo-random bus stalls, a 7.75\npercent reduction. The canonical five CRCs, validation literal,\nEBREAK completion and OOB check all pass. Unchanged selftest and three\nrandom-program RVFI cosim comparisons also pass with both bus stalls.\nOn the corrected scalar-to\n…[3480 of 6552 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:ffc23187b8295d27]…\neal changing-return-target errors, insufficient headroom for a return\nstack alone. Scratch prototypes moving target/inverse calculations\ndirectly into ID preserved 4,193,876 CoreMark cycles and canonical CRCs,\nbut reduced median Gowin Fmax to 78.978 MHz, or 67.343 MHz with RAM16\nbanking. Their critical path became BTB lookup followed by inverse\narithmetic into ID/EX. This identifies the better predictor angle:\ncache comparison operands during resolved training, so neither EX\nforwarding nor the current fetch lookup feeds a serial carry chain\nbefore prediction validation.\n\nhyp-20260930-003-r11s2 Verify next-PC predictions from the registered EX/MEM successor regression 173.18 4193876\nhyp-20260930-003-r12s2 Compact operand certificates for next-PC prediction verification broken None None\nhyp-20260930-003-r13s2 Validate predicted successors with parallel carry consistency regression 220.65 4193876\nhyp-20260930-003-r14s2 Verify predicted control targets with short parallel carry segments regression 223.04 4193876\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
