{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_13", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor l in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(l)\n if d.get('id','').endswith(('r5s2','r6s2','r9s2')):\n  print(d['id'])\n  print('RESULT',d.get('fitness'),d.get('cycles'),d.get('fmax_mhz'),d.get('critical_path'))\n  print('PROPOSAL',d.get('hypothesis',{}).get('hypothesis',''))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20260930-003-r5s2\nRESULT 149.28 3919730 58.513 {'from': 'cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s', 'to': 'dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -13.193, 'arrival_ns': 23.488, 'logic_cells': 17, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\nPROPOSAL Add one branch-discovered loop stream predictor to if_stage, retaining\nthe champion's existing BTB, immediate EX resolution and one-entry\nfall-through skid buffer. A valid, advancing, legal, aligned, taken\nconditional backward branch identifies a replay region from its target\nthrough its branch PC, inclusive. Accept only regions of at most 64\naligned instruction words: branch PC minus target at most 252 bytes.\nTrack one region with full 32-bit base/end PCs, region validity and\n64 per-word fill-valid bits. Allocate only branch-discovered loop regions.\n\nRegister a separate copy of EX feedback for loop discovery only.\nCapture payload each clock and clear validity on reset; consume each\nvalid update once on the following edge. Compute backward direction,\nspan and descriptor replacement from that registered copy. Keep\noriginal BTB training and immediate EX recovery unchanged. Changing\nthe descriptor invalidates every replay slot; repeated resolution of\nthe same loop retains filled slots. Never hold and replay a valid\ndiscovery update during fetch or execution stalls.\n\nFill an unreset 64-by-32 instruction array only from real accepted\nimemReady responses whose full fetch PC lies inside the current region.\nIndex slots by PC[7:2]. A contiguous region of at most 64 words has no\nrepeated index, including across a 256-byte boundary. Reset validity\nonly. Use distributed asynchronous-read storage for this small replay\narray to avoid adding another predictor-side BSRAM address endpoint;\ndo not alter the existing BTB storage or arithmetic. Keep the common\nready-bus data path shallow, and keep discovery off payload enables.\nDescriptor replacement clears slot validity even with a simultaneous\nold-region fill; payload written on that edge must remain invalid.\n\nPrefer\n…[13768 of 16840 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:50dc1a85fe2a8bb8]…\n exact\ncaptured predictions through stalls, and resolution of every valid\ninstruction against its architectural successor. Keep the champion's\ncomplete ALU operand choices, blocking M arithmetic, decoder default\nlegality, alignment traps, bus protocol and nret=1 RVFI contract.\n\nThe prototype's cycle count includes registered-queue refill and\nrecovery latency. At 3,868,725 cycles, exceeding the champion by the\nrequired 4.6 percent needs median Fmax above 84.758 MHz. Its measured\n87.662 MHz clears that threshold, supporting an eight percent expected\nfitness gain with medium confidence. Prototype evidence is not an\naccepted tournament result. The principal risks are formal correctness\nin FIFO/replay invalidation corners and implementation drift that\nrestores tag-before-comparison selection or fetch/hazard feedback.\nVerify actual RAM mapping, all unchanged formal/cosim gates,\ncanonical CoreMark CRCs and validation literal with both standard bus\nstalls, marker-only cycles, OOB checks and all-option Gowin median.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
