{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_15", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor l in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(l)\n if d.get('id')=='hyp-20260930-001-r9s0': print(json.dumps(d,indent=2)[-8500:])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "6.702 ns across twelve\\ncells. Accepted operand preselection has removed serial forwarding\\ndecisions, leaving ordinary ALU implementation as a timing opportunity.\\nExisting SLL/SRL/SRA use separate dynamic shift expressions. Prior\\nmicro_opt history supports shortening combinational paths at unchanged\\ninstruction cycles; the sibling result-ownership partition did not\\nbeat the current champion. A local grouped shifter is a distinct angle.\\n\",\n    \"hypothesis\": \"Replace only ordinary shift implementation in alu.sv with explicit\\nradix-4 grouped barrel networks. Keep the binary operation encoding,\\nexisting ALU ports, complete registered operand selections, pipeline\\nboundaries and instruction latencies unchanged. There is no additional\\nregister, stall, prediction policy or execution stage.\\n\\nBuild separate left and right data networks, each with three steps.\\nDecode b[1:0] into low_sel = 4'b0001 << b[1:0] and b[3:2] into\\nmid_sel = 4'b0001 << b[3:2]. The first step selects shifts of 0/1/2/3\\nbits; the second selects 0/4/8/12 bits; the final step selects 0/16\\nbits using b[4]. Express each four-way step as an OR of four data\\nterms masked by the mutually exclusive selector bits. Use fixed slices\\nand concatenations rather than variable shift expressions inside the\\nnetwork. Left shifts always fill zero. Both SRL and SRA share the\\nright network, with fill = (op == ALU_SRA) && a[31]; each fixed right\\nshift concatenates the required number of copies of this original fill\\nbit. Right fill remains correct through both grouped steps and the\\nfinal sixteen-bit step. No input/output bit reversal is needed.\\n\\nRoute ALU_SLL to the final left word and ALU_SRL/ALU_SRA to the final\\nright word inside the established operation-result case. Preserve\\nevery other case arm, full-width ADD/SUB/compare semantics, default\\nzero result, real MUL/DIV algorithms, ownership, request/completion\\nhandshakes, operand capture and exact RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS formulas.\\nDo not add one-hot operation payload fields or modify ID/EX layouts.\\n\n…[5429 of 8501 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:937df8becdf91c89]…\n  ],\n  \"perturbations\": [\n    [\n      0,\n      92.907,\n      11\n    ],\n    [\n      1,\n      93.708,\n      10\n    ],\n    [\n      2,\n      93.708,\n      10\n    ]\n  ],\n  \"lutram\": 32,\n  \"bsram\": 7,\n  \"dsp\": 2,\n  \"critical_path\": {\n    \"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.write_value_14_s0\",\n    \"to\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.fwd_rs2_sel_1_s0\",\n    \"slack_ns\": -5.763,\n    \"arrival_ns\": 16.058,\n    \"logic_cells\": 25,\n    \"modules\": [\n      \"clock_ibuf\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex\",\n      \"cpu/u_fwd\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"logic_levels\": 11,\n  \"formal_passed\": true,\n  \"cosim_passed\": true,\n  \"error\": null,\n  \"implementation_notes\": \"\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-30T04:33:47.314900Z\",\n  \"slot\": 0,\n  \"round_id\": 9,\n  \"lesson\": \"- 2026-09-30 hyp-20260930-001-r9s0 (improvement, +6.68%): Grouping fixed-slice shifts into 0/1/2/3, 0/4/8/12 and 0/16 mask-and-OR stages and sharing SRL/SRA routing with op-gated original sign fill shortens ALU timing and reduces LUT4 use at unchanged CoreMark cycles, leaving forwarding and predictor paths as the next timing limits.\"\n}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
