turn {'passed': True, 'retired': len(ref_trace)}\ntest/cosim/run_cosim.py:104:    # --dstall to run the trace comparison under bus backpressure).\ntest/cosim/main.cpp:27:static bool oob_access = false;  // sticky: once set, final marker reports it\ntest/cosim/main.cpp:32:// Benchmark-time MMIO markers. CoreMark's portme.c writes to BENCH_START\ntest/cosim/main.cpp:70:    //           (tools/eval/fpga.py:run_coremark_ipc) passes BOTH so t\n…[11211 of 14283 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:db256124c9ec4178]…\n   elif fn7 == 0x20:\n                v = (a-b) if fn3 == 0 else (self.sx(a, 32) >> (b & 31)) & MASK\n            else:  # fn7 == 0x01 (M-extension)\n                if   fn3 == 0: v = (sa * sb) & MASK\n                elif fn3 == 1: v = ((sa * sb) >> 32) & MASK\n                elif fn3 == 2: v = ((sa * b) >> 32) & MASK\n                elif fn3 == 3: v = ((a * b) >> 32) & MASK\n                elif fn3 == 4: v = MASK if b == 0 else (\n                    0x80000000 if sa == -2**31 and sb == -1\n                    else self.trunc_div(sa, sb) & MASK)\n                elif fn3 == 5: v = MASK if b == 0 else a // b\n                elif fn3 == 6: v = a if b == 0 else (\n                    0 if sa == -2**31 and sb == -1\n                    else self.trunc_rem(sa, sb) & MASK)\n                else:          v = a if b == 0 else a % b\n            return self._retire(**trap_kwargs, wrd=rd, wval=v & MASK)\n\n        if op == 0x13:  # OP-IMM\n            a = r[rs1]\n            # Shift funct3 (1, 5) requires specific funct7 values.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(line)\n print(d.get('id'),d.get('category'),d.get('outcome'),d.get('fitness'),d.get('cycles'))\n if d.get('category')=='predictor' or d.get('id')=='hyp-20260929-001-r4s0':\n  print('Title:', d.get('title'))\n  print('Motivation:',d.get('motivation'))\n  h=d.get('hypothesis');print('Hypothesis:', h.get('hypothesis') if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\n  print('Notes:',d.get('implementation_notes'))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(line)\n print(d.get('id'),d.get('category'),d.get('outcome'),d.get('fitness'),d.get('cycles'))\n if d.get('category')=='predictor' or d.get('id')=='hyp-20260929-001-r4s0':\n  print('Title:', d.get('title'))\n  print('Motivation:',d.get('motivation'))\n  h=d.get('hypothesis');print('Hypothesis:', h.get('hypothesis') if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\n  print('Notes:',d.get('implementation_notes'))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "baseline-bench-9c56dde micro_opt improvement 12.12 4491485\nhyp-20260929-001-r1s0 micro_opt regression 13.35 4491485\nhyp-20260929-002-r1s1 structural improvement 110.0 4491817\nhyp-20260929-003-r1s2 predictor regression 13.07 4197517\nTitle: 64-entry tagged next-PC predictor with two-bit branch direction\nMotivation: The baseline fetches sequentially and flushes the combinational IF/ID\ninstruction whenever EX resolves a taken branch or jump. Because IF/ID\nis not registered, each such transfer loses one fetch/decode opportunity,\nrather than the two bubbles suggested by the five-stage comments.\nCoreMark repeatedly executes loop branches and call sites, making these\nbubbles a promising source of cycle savings. The measured 199.837 ns\ncritical path is through forwarding and the combinational ALU; a small\nPC-indexed predictor should improve iterations/cycle without adding\nlogic to that arithmetic path. No predictor experiments or lessons are\npresent in this fixture's history.\n\nA fresh architectural trace of the canonical -O3, RV32IM, 2K,\nten-iteration CoreMark ELF contains 2,922,016 bracketed instructions,\n529,588 conditional branches, 49,367 JALs, and 13,735 JALRs. Sequential\nprediction would mispredict 357,527 next PCs. A 64-entry tagged table\nwith this policy reduces next-PC errors to 62,551; 32 entries give\n73,619 errors and 128 entries give 58,167. Thus 64 entries capture most\nof the available benefit without doubling storage for only 4,384 fewer\nerrors. This trace model uses immediate training and no speculative\npipeline or bus timing, so it supports the sizing decision rather than\nconstituting a measured RTL speedup.\n\nHypothesis: Add one 64-entry direct-mapped tagged branch-target buffer in if_stage.\nIndex with fetch PC[7:2]; each entry holds a valid bit, PC[31:8] tag,\naligned 30-bit target, unconditional-transfer bit, and a two-bit\nsaturating conditional-branch counter. Reset valid bits only, keeping\npayload arrays free of reset to permit distributed-memory inference.\nA matching unconditional entry or conditional \n…[26881 of 29953 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:dd0c64589ef2c092]…\nd need not be reset.\nA held EX instruction still trains only once when it advances, and\nbuffered tokens must preserve order through imem/dmem stalls and\nblocking arithmetic completion.\n\nExpect approximately six percent higher fitness from fewer fetch\nbubbles, with low confidence until measured. At unchanged Fmax, beating\nthe 4.6 percent acceptance threshold requires fewer than approximately\n4,192,084 bracketed cycles, a saving of roughly 193,000 cycles. Six\npercent improvement corresponds to approximately 4,136,717 cycles.\nThese are break-even calculations, not measured buffer results.\nThe token-selection mux may lower Fmax and a one-entry buffer may hide\ntoo few stalls; measure vendor median timing and actual marker cycles\ntogether. Preserve canonical CRCs, memory bounds, decoder legality,\nnret=1 and all RVFI invariants. Run unchanged formal/cosim/CoreMark\ngates. This hypothesis changes predictor-guided fetch scheduling only;\ndo not combine it with the rejected training, storage or recovery trials.\n\nNotes: \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
