{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/test/test_if_stage.py'", "aggregated_output": "\"\"\"PC-only predictor and elastic, fall-through fetch acceptance.\"\"\"\nimport random\n\nimport cocotb\nfrom cocotb.triggers import Timer\n\nfrom _helpers import run_cocotb\n\n\ndef _update(pc, target=0, *, valid=1, allocate=1, unconditional=0, taken=1):\n    flags = (valid << 3) | (allocate << 2) | (unconditional << 1) | taken\n    return (flags << 64) | (pc << 32) | target\n\n\ndef _prediction(dut):\n    return (int(dut.out.value) >> 33) & 0xFFFFFFFF\n\n\ndef _token(dut):\n    value = int(dut.out.value)\n    return ((value >> 65) & 0xFFFFFFFF, (value >> 33) & 0xFFFFFFFF,\n            (value >> 1) & 0xFFFFFFFF, value & 1)\n\n\nasync def _tick(dut):\n    dut.clock.value = 0\n    await Timer(5, \"ns\")\n    dut.clock.value = 1\n    await Timer(5, \"ns\")\n    dut.clock.value = 0\n    await Timer(1, \"ns\")\n\n\nasync def _setup(dut):\n    dut.clock.value = 0\n    dut.reset.value = 1\n    dut.stall.value = 1\n    # Predictor-only tests must not enqueue fetches during their ID holds.\n    dut.imem_ready.value = 0\n    dut.redirect.value = 0\n    dut.redirect_target.value = 0\n    dut.imem_data.value = 0xDEADBEEF\n    dut.update.value = 0\n    await _tick(dut)\n    dut.reset.value = 0\n\n\nasync def _at(dut, pc):\n    dut.redirect.value = 1\n    dut.redirect_target.value = pc\n    await _tick(dut)\n    dut.redirect.value = 0\n    await Timer(1, \"ns\")\n    assert int(dut.imem_addr.value) == pc\n\n\nasync def _train(dut, pc, target=0, **flags):\n    dut.update.value = _update(pc, target, **flags)\n    await _tick(dut)\n    dut.update.value = 0\n    await Timer(1, \"ns\")\n\n\n@cocotb.test()\nasync def counters_saturate_and_lookup_has_no_update_bypass(dut):\n    await _setup(dut)\n    await _at(dut, 0x40)\n    assert _prediction(dut) == 0x44\n    dut.update.value = _update(0x40, 0x100)\n    await Timer(1, \"ns\")\n    assert _prediction(dut) == 0x44, \"allocation bypassed the pre-edge table\"\n    await _tick(dut)\n    dut.update.value = 0\n    await Timer(1, \"ns\")\n    assert _prediction(dut) == 0x100  # new taken branch is weak taken\n    for taken, expected in [(1, 0x100), (1, 0x100), (0, 0x100),\n        \n…[7577 of 10649 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:40f1927850812a25]…\ned = queued or raw\n        assert int(dut.imem_addr.value) == pc\n        assert _token(dut) == offered\n        if reset or recovery:\n            pc, queued = (0 if reset else target), None\n            pending.clear()\n        else:\n            accept = ready and (queued is None or not stalled)\n            if accept:\n                pending.append(raw)\n            if offered[3] and not stalled:\n                assert pending.pop(0) == offered, \"duplicate or reordered acceptance\"\n                assert offered[2] not in consumed\n                consumed.add(offered[2])\n            if accept and (queued is not None or stalled):\n                queued = raw\n            elif not stalled:\n                queued = None\n            if accept:\n                pc += 4\n        await _tick(dut)\n    assert len(consumed) > 300, \"insufficient progress in randomized fetch test\"\n\n\ndef test_if_stage_runner():\n    run_cocotb(toplevel=\"if_stage\", sources=[\"core_pkg.sv\", \"if_stage.sv\"],\n               test_module=\"test_if_stage\")\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d['category']=='predictor':\n  print(d['id'],d['title'], 'fitness',d.get('fitness'),'cycles',d.get('cycles'),'MHz',d.get('fmax_mhz'))\n  h=d.get('hypothesis',{})\n  if isinstance(h,dict): print(h.get('motivation','')[:1400])\n  print('PATH', d.get('critical_path'))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20260929-003-r1s2 64-entry tagged next-PC predictor with two-bit branch direction fitness 13.07 cycles 4197517 MHz 5.487\nThe baseline fetches sequentially and flushes the combinational IF/ID\ninstruction whenever EX resolves a taken branch or jump. Because IF/ID\nis not registered, each such transfer loses one fetch/decode opportunity,\nrather than the two bubbles suggested by the five-stage comments.\nCoreMark repeatedly executes loop branches and call sites, making these\nbubbles a promising source of cycle savings. The measured 199.837 ns\ncritical path is through forwarding and the combinational ALU; a small\nPC-indexed predictor should improve iterations/cycle without adding\nlogic to that arithmetic path. No predictor experiments or lessons are\npresent in this fixture's history.\n\nA fresh architectural trace of the canonical -O3, RV32IM, 2K,\nten-iteration CoreMark ELF contains 2,922,016 bracketed instructions,\n529,588 conditional branches, 49,367 JALs, and 13,735 JALRs. Sequential\nprediction would mispredict 357,527 next PCs. A 64-entry tagged table\nwith this policy reduces next-PC errors to 62,551; 32 entries give\n73,619 errors and 128 entries give 58,167. Thus 64 entries capture most\nof the available benefit without doubling storage for only 4,384 fewer\nerrors. This trace model uses immediate training and no speculative\npipeline or bus timing, so it supports the sizing decision rather than\nconstituting a measured RTL speedup.\n\nPATH {